var SPS={};
var SPC={"Accursed":{"size":"Small or Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Accursed vary a great deal. Some look like another folk and age much as they do. Odd ones age fast or live ageless until something kills them."],["Unique Nature","Accursed have no traditional traits. Your origin or kind sets your traits, so choose any eight. If you look like or once lived as a standard heritage, you may start from that heritage's traditional traits."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: none, any eight traits of your choice. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. If you are Small, you can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Arisen":{"size":"Small or Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Some Arisen age slowly, with their made bodies shrugging off age. Others wear out faster. They may live into their second or third century or fade before 60."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Magical Fortification, Tenacious, Toughness. Exploration: Artificial Form, Inured to the Elements. Roleplaying: Embrace the Past, Magical Insight, Unnatural Healer. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. If you are Small, you can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Dhampir (Grim Hollow)":{"size":"Small or Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","The curse makes a Dhampir ageless. They can still die in many other ways."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Draining Attack, Natural Attack (Fangs), Well Protected. Exploration: Climber, Darkvision. Roleplaying: Eager Deceiver, Magical Savvy (Charm Person), Magical Savvy (Friends). You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. If you are Small, you can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Disembodied":{"size":"Small or Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Disembodied age far slower than the folk they were, with a life expectancy two or three times as long."],["Insubstantial","You look like a translucent copy of your former self and weigh a quarter of what you did."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Magical Fortification, Master of Distraction, Out of Phase. Exploration: Ethereal Fade, Inured to the Elements. Roleplaying: Magical Insight, Magical Savvy (Feather Fall), Magical Savvy (Dancing Lights). You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. If you are Small, you can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Downcast":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Without immortality the Downcast still live long. They mature in their late teens and can reach 800 years."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Divine Sangromancy, Touch of Life. Exploration: Inured to the Elements, Meditative Rest, Tireless. Roleplaying: Magical Savvy (Cleric spells only), Magical Savvy (Thaumaturgy), Moved by Faith. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Dragonborn (Grim Hollow)":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Dragonborn grow quickly. They walk hours after hatching, look like a 10-year-old human child at 3, and are adults at 15. They live about 80 years."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Breath Weapon, Damage Resistance (same type as the Breath Weapon), Menacing Roar. Exploration: Darkvision, Natural Movement, Powerful Build. Roleplaying: Firm Influence, Moved by Faith. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Dreamer":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","The stasis magic that held the Dreamers during their long sleep kept their bodies from aging. They mature at 18 and live to 250."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Quick Initiative, Stalwart Reserves. Exploration: Darkvision, Helping Hand, Power Nap. Roleplaying: Dreamwalking, Improviser, Inborn Perception. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Dwarf (Grim Hollow)":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Dwarves mature physically in their late teens but count as young until 50. They live about 350 years."],["Heavy Armor Pace","Wearing Heavy armor does not reduce your Speed."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Damage Resistance (Poison), Toughness, Weapon Aptitude. Exploration: Darkvision, Poison Resilience, Steady. Roleplaying: Artisanal Focus (Brewer's Supplies, Mason's Tools or Smith's Tools), Crafter's Eye. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. You can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Elf (Grim Hollow)":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Elves reach physical maturity like humans do, but claim adulthood and an adult name around 100. They live to 750."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Awakened Mind, Focused Mind, Weapon Aptitude. Exploration: Darkvision, Meditative Rest, Shroud of the Wild. Roleplaying: Inborn Perception, Magical Savvy (any cantrip). You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Gnome (Grim Hollow)":{"size":"Small","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Gnomes are physically mature at 18 and expected to settle into adult life around 40. They live almost 500 years."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Magical Fortification, Quick Slip. Exploration: Artifice Expertise, Darkvision, Fade Away. Roleplaying: Magical Savvy (any cantrip), Masterful Aptitude, Nature's Voice. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. You can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Grudgel":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Grudgels reach adulthood around 16 and live into their seventh decade or longer."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Battlefield Control, Centered. Exploration: Darkvision, Powerful Build, Tireless. Roleplaying: Artisanal Focus, Impromptu Artisan, Magical Savvy (any cantrip). You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Halfling (Grim Hollow)":{"size":"Small","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","A Halfling is an adult at 20 and usually lives to the middle of a second century."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Brave, Creature Cover, Lucky. Exploration: Helping Hand, Pass Through, Power Nap. Roleplaying: Artisanal Focus (Brewer's Supplies, Cook's Utensils or Potter's Tools), Embrace the Past. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. You can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Human (Grim Hollow)":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Humans reach adulthood in their late teens and live less than a century."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Awesome Critical, First Strike, Weapon Aptitude. Exploration: Helping Hand, Intrinsic Orientation. Roleplaying: Artisanal Focus, Keen Survivor, Skill Prowess. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Laneshi":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Laneshi mature fast, reaching adulthood around 14, and live up to 150 years."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Awakened Mind, Psychic Spirit. Exploration: Amphibious, Darkvision, Swimmer. Roleplaying: Animal Friend, Magical Savvy (any Necromancy cantrip), Nature's Voice. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24","fx":{"moves":{"swim":30}}},"Ogresh":{"size":"Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Ogresh reach maturity around 25 but stay youthful for decades after. They live up to 300 years."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Enemy in Motion, Focused Mind. Exploration: Environmental Awareness, Natural Movement, Powerful Build. Roleplaying: Calculating Listener, Commanding Insight, Persuasive Knack. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Wechselkind":{"size":"Small","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Wechselkind do not age normally. They stay in their doll-like shape, their lifespan is set by wear and damage, and magical aging cannot touch them."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Creature Cover, Magical Fortification. Exploration: Artificial Form, Helping Hand, Pass Through. Roleplaying: Magical Savvy (Disguise Self), Magical Savvy (Minor Illusion), Intuitive Acrobat. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. You can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"},"Wulven":{"size":"Small or Medium","speed":30,"dark":0,"type":"Humanoid","traits":[["Age","Wulven mature like the folk they were before the curse, but its magic eases the harm of old age and they stay fit late into life."],["Heritage Traits","Pick eight traits from the Heritage Traits list. The traditional picks for this heritage are: Combat: Hunter's Instinct, Natural Attack (Claws), Pack Hunter. Exploration: Burst of Speed, Climber. Roleplaying: Athlete's Spirit, Inborn Perception, Nature's Voice. You can swap any traditional trait for another from the pool, take a trait twice for its second effect, or use the traditional traits of another heritage. If you are Small, you can lower your Speed by 5 feet to gain one extra trait."]],"opts":{"label":"Heritage Traits","n":8,"list":[["Amphibious","(Exploration) You breathe air and water. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws made while submerged. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Animal Friend","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Animal Handling. **Second pick.** Advantage on Animal Handling checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artifice Expertise","(Combat and Exploration) Proficiency with Tinker's Tools. You can spend 10 minutes and 10 GP of materials to build a palm-sized clockwork device with one function. Smoker: fills a 5-foot Cube with smoke for 1 minute and makes it Lightly Obscured. Lighter: a candle-sized flame that lights flammable things. Compass: always points north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. **Second pick.** Building a device takes 1 minute. A device can also get the Distractor function (Combat): as a Bonus Action you place or throw it into a space within 30 feet. A creature in its space makes a DC 10 Intelligence save. On a failure, attacks against that creature have Advantage until the start of your next turn. A creature can use an action to destroy it. Up to three of your devices can have it, and you reset that on a Long Rest.",{}],["Artificial Form","(Exploration) You are a Construct, yet healing spells still work on you and you can spend Hit Point Dice on rests as normal. You need no food, drink, sleep or air, but you still need 8 hours of inactivity for a Long Rest. **Second pick.** When Mending is cast on you, you can spend a Hit Point Die and regain the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Artisanal Focus","(Roleplaying) Choose an Artisan's Tools set and gain proficiency with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with a new Artisan's Tools set. You also have Advantage on checks with every tool chosen this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Athlete's Spirit","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Athletics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Athletics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Awakened Mind","(Combat) You automatically succeed on saves against magical effects that would make you Incapacitated, Stunned or Unconscious. This does not cover falling Unconscious from dropping to 0 Hit Points. **Second pick.** You also have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.",{}],["Awesome Critical","(Combat) When you score a Critical Hit with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike, roll one extra damage die of the weapon and add it to the critical damage. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can add the maximum of the weapon's original dice and the extra die instead of rolling them. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Battlefield Control","(Combat) Creatures provoke an Opportunity Attack from you when they move into your reach, as well as when they leave it. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Opportunity Attacks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Born Healer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Medicine. **Second pick.** Advantage on Medicine checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Brave","(Combat) Advantage on saves to avoid the Frightened condition. **Second pick.** As a Reaction, you give one ally who can see or hear you Advantage on a save against being Frightened. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Breath Weapon","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, and choose a 5-foot by 30-foot Line or a 15-foot Cone. As a Magic action you breathe it. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Constitution modifier + Proficiency Bonus). A target takes 1d8 of the chosen type on a failure, or half on a success. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives another breath weapon with its own uses, damage type and area. When you use any breath weapon, one target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save. This part resets on a Long Rest.",{}],["Burst of Speed","(Exploration) On your turn you can add 30 feet to your Speed until the end of that turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** On a turn when you use it, you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",{}],["Calculating Listener","(Roleplaying) After talking with a nonhostile creature for at least 1 minute, you can try to charm it. It makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Charisma modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is Charmed for 1 hour. The GM may also have it reveal one fact it knows about the topic. The target never learns you tried, whether it saves or not. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save, and a failed save lasts 8 hours.",{}],["Centered","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or ability check you make before the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When that roll succeeds, choose one creature within 30 feet. It has Advantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn.",{}],["Charging Attack","(Combat) If you move at least 20 feet straight at a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack or an Unarmed Strike on the same turn, you can attack it again as a Bonus Action with the same weapon. **Second pick.** After the charging movement, your attacks have Advantage until the end of your turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Climber","(Exploration) You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** You can climb up, down, across vertical surfaces and upside down on ceilings with your hands free. While climbing you can Dash as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{"moves":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Commanding Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Insight. **Second pick.** Advantage on Insight checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Connection to Nature","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Nature. **Second pick.** Advantage on Nature checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Crafter's Eye","(Roleplaying) On a History check about an object (an item, device, building or material), if you are proficient with an Artisan's Tools set used to make it, you count as proficient in History and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on those History checks. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Creature Cover","(Combat) You can take the Hide action while behind a creature that is larger than you, even though it only gives you Cover. **Second pick.** You can also hide behind a creature of your own size.",{}],["Damage Resistance","(Combat) Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. You have Resistance to that damage type. **Second pick.** As a Reaction when you take damage of the chosen type, you gain Immunity to it until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Short Rest.",{}],["Darkvision","(Exploration) Darkvision out to 60 feet. In Dim Light you see as if it were Bright Light, in Darkness as if it were Dim Light, and in Darkness you see only shades of gray. **Second pick.** The range becomes 120 feet.",{"dark":60}],["Divine Sangromancy","(Combat) When an ally within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can spend a Hit Point Die and add the roll to the healing. **Second pick.** When you use it, you also regain Hit Points equal to the roll.",{}],["Draining Attack","(Combat) This works with the Natural Attack trait. When you hit with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **Second pick.** The target's Hit Point maximum also drops by the damage dealt. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Dreamwalking","(Roleplaying) While you rest, you absorb thoughts and memories from the dreams of those near you. You have Advantage on ability checks to recall lore or knowledge. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Using a Search action on a creature you can see, you make a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a success you learn one secret of the GM's choice that it knows. A creature without a language gives you only vague images. Regained on a Short Rest or Long Rest.",{}],["Driver","(Exploration) Proficiency with Navigator's Tools, and Advantage on ability checks to drive a vehicle. **Second pick.** Driving checks that need an action cost you no action. This free use works once per round.",{}],["Eager Deceiver","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Deception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Deception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Embrace the Past","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in History. **Second pick.** Advantage on History checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Enemy in Motion","(Combat) When you make an attack roll against a creature, or a save against its attack, spell or ability, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage if that creature moved since the end of your last turn. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** The Reaction can also give the same Advantage to an ally within 30 feet.",{}],["Environmental Awareness","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. While there, on checks to assess structures, monuments or natural features, find food or drinkable water, or track creatures, you count as proficient in the fitting skill and add double your Proficiency Bonus. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds a new environment. You also have Advantage on checks made with this trait. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Ethereal Fade","(Exploration) As a Magic action you fade into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. You cannot interact with the Material Plane and nothing there can affect you, spells and creatures included. You can move and hear as normal and you see in shades of gray. When it ends you return to the nearest free space to where you left. You can end it early as a Bonus Action. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Wisdom checks made as part of a Search action.",{}],["Even in Sleep","(Exploration) While you sleep (Unconscious from sleep), you stay aware of your surroundings and can make Perception checks as normal. **Second pick.** While asleep you automatically sense any creature within 30 feet that means you harm. A creature that is merely able to harm you does not count until it intends to.",{}],["Fade Away","(Exploration) As a Bonus Action you take the Hide action without needing Heavy Obscurement or Cover, and you need not be out of sight. You become visible at the start of your next turn unless you moved into a spot where you could hide normally. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the check, and you stay hidden until the end of your next turn instead.",{}],["Firm Influence","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Intimidation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Intimidation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["First Strike","(Combat) When you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the combat, the hit deals an extra 2d6 damage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can use the maximum of the extra dice instead of rolling. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Fleet of Foot","(Exploration) Your Speed rises by 5 feet. **Second pick.** Your Speed rises by another 5 feet (10 in total). As a Bonus Action you also give any number of creatures within 30 feet +10 feet of Speed for 1 minute. Regained on a Long Rest.",{"speed":5}],["Focused Mind","(Combat) Advantage on saves against the Charmed condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Charmed, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Focused Reserves","(Combat) As a Reaction after you take damage, roll a number of d6 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can reroll 1s and 2s when you use it, but you must keep the new rolls.",{}],["Gifted Performer","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Performance. **Second pick.** Advantage on Performance checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Helping Hand","(Exploration and Combat) You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action to aid an ally's ability check (Exploration). **Second pick.** You can also aid an ally's attack roll with it (Combat). Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Hold Breath","(Exploration) You can hold your breath for 1 hour. **Second pick.** You can hold your breath for 8 hours.",{}],["Hunter's Instinct","(Combat) At the end of each Long Rest you gain a number of d8 equal to your Proficiency Bonus. When you attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one d8 and add it to the attack roll or the damage roll. For the attack roll you can decide after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known. **Second pick.** If you add the d8 to an attack roll and the attack misses, you keep the d8.",{}],["Impromptu Artisan","(Roleplaying) With Artisan's Tools you are proficient with, and suitable raw materials and equipment (the GM decides), you can use a Short Rest to craft one nonmagical item worth 10 GP or less. It can be adventuring gear, a weapon or shield, or a simple unique item the GM approves. It works but is not high quality and cannot be sold unless the GM allows. **Second pick.** You can instead craft during a Long Rest, with an item worth up to 50 GP.",{}],["Improviser","(Roleplaying) As a Bonus Action, choose a skill or tool you lack proficiency in. You are proficient with it for 1 hour. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks using the skill or tool you picked. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inborn Perception","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Perception. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instinctive Stealth","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Stealth. **Second pick.** Advantage on Stealth checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Instrumentalist","(Roleplaying) Proficiency with one Musical Instrument of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with two new instruments. You also have Advantage on checks with any instrument. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Intrinsic Orientation","(Exploration) You always know which way is north, or a cardinal direction the GM picks on another plane. You have Advantage on ability checks to avoid getting lost, to navigate or to track. **Second pick.** When you fail one of those checks, you can choose to succeed. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Intuitive Acrobat","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Acrobatics. **Second pick.** Advantage on Acrobatics checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Inured to the Elements","(Exploration) Advantage on Constitution saves against extreme cold or extreme heat. **Second pick.** You automatically succeed on those saves.",{}],["Irrepressible Sight","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Blinded condition. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Blinded, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Keen Survivor","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Survival. **Second pick.** Advantage on Survival checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Larger Target","(Combat) When you hit a creature one size larger than you, you can deal extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** It works on a creature of any larger size.",{}],["Light Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Light armor. **Second pick.** Your AC rises by 1 while you wear Light armor.",{}],["Lucky","(Combat) When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you can reroll and must use the new roll. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the reroll.",{}],["Magical Fortification","(Combat) Choose an ability score. You have Advantage on saves with it against spells and other magical effects. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new ability score. If you fail a save against a spell or magical effect and lack proficiency in that save, you can use a Reaction to reroll it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Insight","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Arcana. **Second pick.** Advantage on Arcana checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Magical Savvy","(Roleplaying) Learn one cantrip from any spell list. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence for Wizard spells, Wisdom for Cleric and Druid spells and Charisma for Bard, Sorcerer and Warlock spells. If the spell is on several lists, pick one list to set the ability. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives a new cantrip, or a level 1 spell from the same list as a cantrip you already took. You cast a level 1 spell once without a slot and regain that on a Long Rest. If you have levels in the matching class, it is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells.",{}],["Master of Distraction","(Combat) As an Influence action you put on a show (bravado, cowardice, confusion or similar). Until the end of your next turn, attacks against an enemy within 10 feet of you that could see you take the action have Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** One affected enemy of your choice also has Disadvantage on attack rolls against your allies until the end of your next turn.",{}],["Masterful Aptitude","(Roleplaying) Choose a skill or tool you are proficient with. You have Expertise on checks with it. **Second pick.** Each extra pick covers a new proficiency. You also have Advantage on checks with those. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Meditative Rest","(Exploration) You rest by meditating for 4 hours, dreaming but awake. This gives the benefit other humanoids get from 8 hours of sleep. **Second pick.** You need only 2 hours. At the end of each Long Rest you also gain a d6. Before your next Long Rest ends, you can add it to a D20 Test, deciding after the d20 is rolled but before the result is known.",{}],["Medium Armor Training","(Combat) Training with Medium armor and Shields. **Second pick.** Training with Heavy armor.",{}],["Menacing Roar","(Combat) As a Bonus Action you let out a roar or shout. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet that can hear you makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Constitution modifier) or is Frightened until the end of your next turn. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** One target of your choice has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mighty Shove","(Combat) When you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee attack, you can use a Bonus Action to shove it. It makes a Strength or Dexterity save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or is pushed up to 10 feet away. **Second pick.** The target has Disadvantage on the save.",{}],["Mindful Investigator","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Investigation. **Second pick.** Advantage on Investigation checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Moved by Faith","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Religion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Religion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Attack","(Combat) Your Unarmed Strike deals 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. Choose Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing to fit your natural weapons (claws, horns, tail, fangs and so on). **Second pick.** You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Camouflage","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide there. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. When you Hide in any of them, you can skip the roll and treat it as a 15. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Natural Movement","(Exploration) Choose an environment: arctic, coastal, desert, forest, grassland, hill and mountain, swamp, subterranean or underwater. There, nonmagical Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement and checks to track you have Disadvantage. **Second pick.** Each extra pick adds an environment. In any of them, as a Bonus Action, you can give the benefit for 1 hour to creatures of your choice who stay within 120 feet and can see you.",{}],["Nature's Voice","(Roleplaying) You can share simple ideas with Beasts and Plant creatures through sounds and gestures, such as whether they are hungry. You gain no control over them and learn no detailed information. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on ability checks made as part of an Influence action toward a Beast or Plant.",{}],["Nimble Moves","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Sleight of Hand. **Second pick.** Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Out of Phase","(Combat) As a Bonus Action, for 1 minute all creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you and you can move through other creatures' spaces without it counting as Difficult Terrain. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can extend the effect to every ally within 10 feet of you.",{}],["Pack Hunter","(Combat) When an ally within 10 feet is about to make an attack roll or a save, you can use a Reaction to give it Advantage. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** Any ally within 30 feet can trigger it. If the attack misses or the save fails, you do not spend the use.",{}],["Pack Tactics","(Combat) If you start your turn with an ally who is not Incapacitated within 5 feet of another creature you can see, you can use a Reaction to have Advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** Gaining the Advantage takes no action.",{}],["Pass Through","(Exploration) You can move through the space of any creature at least one size larger than you. **Second pick.** Other creatures' spaces are not Difficult Terrain for you.",{}],["Personal Bastion","(Combat) As a Magic action you go still and gain these effects. +4 AC. Disadvantage on Dexterity saves. Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Your Speed is 0 and you cannot gain Speed bonuses. You lose Concentration. You cannot take actions, and your Bonus Action can only end this effect. **Second pick.** Your Speed is halved (rounded down) instead of 0, you do not have Disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you can use your Bonus Action.",{}],["Persuasive Knack","(Roleplaying) Proficiency in Persuasion. **Second pick.** Advantage on Persuasion checks. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Poison Resilience","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being Poisoned. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Poisoned, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Polyglot","(Roleplaying) You learn two languages of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives two more languages. You also have Advantage on Influence checks made in any language you took this way. Uses equal twice your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}],["Power Nap","(Exploration) On a Short Rest you can sleep for 1 hour. If you do, you reduce your Exhaustion by one level and regain one Hit Point Die on top of the usual Short Rest benefits. **Second pick.** When you use it, you can also regain one resource that normally returns on a Long Rest (a Sorcerer could regain a Sorcery Point, for example).",{}],["Powerful Build","(Exploration and Combat) You count as one size larger for carrying, pushing, dragging and lifting. A Small creature with this trait can use weapons with the Heavy property if proficient (Exploration). **Second pick.** When you shove a creature 5 feet or knock it Prone with an Unarmed Strike, the target has Disadvantage on the save (Combat).",{}],["Psychic Spirit","(Combat) Resistance to Psychic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Psychic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Quick Initiative","(Combat) Add your Proficiency Bonus to Initiative rolls. **Second pick.** When you roll Initiative, a result of 9 or lower counts as a 10.",{}],["Quick Slip","(Combat) You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action on each of your turns. You still need suitable cover. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on the Stealth check when you Hide this way.",{}],["Reach Attack","(Combat) Your reach rises by 5 feet. The extra reach does not apply to Opportunity Attacks. **Second pick.** The extra reach applies to Opportunity Attacks too.",{}],["Relentless Endurance","(Combat) When damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points without killing you outright, you drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Regained on a Long Rest. **Second pick.** You drop to 1d6 + your Proficiency Bonus Hit Points instead. You can also use a Reaction to spend up to five Hit Point Dice, roll them and regain that many Hit Points.",{}],["Resilient Ears","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against the Deafened condition. **Second pick.** Advantage on Perception checks that rely on hearing. When you fail a save against being Deafened, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Ruthless Response","(Combat) When a creature within your reach damages you, you can use a Reaction to make a melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against it. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on attack rolls made with it.",{}],["Shroud of the Wild","(Exploration) You can Hide while only Lightly Obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist or similar natural phenomena. **Second pick.** You have Advantage on Stealth checks to Hide this way.",{}],["Skill Prowess","(Roleplaying) Before an ability check with a skill you are proficient in, you can add your Proficiency Bonus a second time. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** When a check made with it fails, you can reroll and must use the new roll.",{}],["Skirmish Tactics","(Combat) When you hit a hostile creature with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, its Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the end of your turn. **Second pick.** After such a hit, you can Disengage as a Bonus Action until the end of your turn.",{}],["Slippery","(Combat) Advantage on Athletics and Acrobatics checks to escape a grapple. **Second pick.** When you fail such a check, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Stalwart Reserves","(Combat) When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can use a Reaction to roll a number of d4 equal to your Proficiency Bonus and gain that many total Temporary Hit Points. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You can take the maximum instead of rolling.",{}],["Standing Leap","(Exploration) Your Long Jump is up to 20 feet and your High Jump up to 10 feet, with or without a running start. You cannot jump farther than your Speed. **Second pick.** Long Jump up to 30 feet and High Jump up to 15 feet, still limited by Speed. Jumping out of a creature's reach does not provoke an Opportunity Attack from it. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Steady","(Exploration) Advantage on saves against being knocked Prone. **Second pick.** Standing up from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement. When you fail a save against being knocked Prone, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Supple Squeeze","(Exploration) You can squeeze through a space meant for a creature two sizes smaller than you, not just one. **Second pick.** Squeezing costs no extra movement, and you have no Disadvantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saves while squeezing.",{}],["Swimmer","(Exploration) You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. **Second pick.** While swimming you can Dash as a Bonus Action.",{"moves":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tenacious","(Combat) Advantage on Death Saving Throws. **Second pick.** When you drop to 0 Hit Points without dying outright, you stay conscious and can act freely. You still make Death Saving Throws, any damage you take adds a failure, and you cannot become Stable while at 0 this way.",{}],["Timely Boon","(Combat) When you fail a save, you can use a Reaction to roll a d4 and add it to the save, which may turn it into a success. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest. **Second pick.** You roll a d8 instead.",{}],["Tireless","(Exploration) Advantage on saves tied to gaining or removing Exhaustion. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against Exhaustion, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Touch of Life","(Combat) Resistance to Necrotic damage. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against an effect that deals Necrotic damage, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Toughness","(Combat) Your Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level. **Second pick.** The bonus is 2 and 2 per level instead. You also have Advantage on saves against effects that lower your Hit Point maximum. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unchecked","(Combat) Advantage on saves against being Restrained. **Second pick.** When you fail a save against being Restrained, you can use a Reaction to succeed instead. Regained on a Long Rest.",{}],["Unnatural Healer","(Roleplaying) During a Long Rest you automatically reverse Grievous Wounds. You can also reattach severed body parts (fingers, legs, tails and so on), restored by the end of the rest. If yours are lost, you can use the matching part of another creature of similar anatomy. You can sever your own parts for swapping with no pain. Unusual parts are up to the GM and give no mechanical benefit beyond other traits. **Second pick.** You also reverse Permanent Wounds during a Long Rest, and you can restore any severed part during a Long Rest as if by Regenerate. Unusual regrown parts are up to the GM.",{}],["Weapon Aptitude","(Combat) Proficiency with three weapons of your choice. **Second pick.** Each extra pick gives proficiency with three new weapons. You also choose one weapon you are proficient with and gain +1 to its damage rolls.",{}],["Well Protected","(Combat) While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier. **Second pick.** When you make a Dexterity save or are targeted by a ranged attack, you can use a Reaction to gain Advantage on the save or impose Disadvantage on the attack. Uses equal your Proficiency Bonus per Long Rest.",{}]]},"hb":"GHPG24"}};
var DFS={};
var SPR=[["Arboreal Curse",7,"Transmutation",["Druid"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"CON","Range 60 ft. Constitution save or Restrained as flesh turns to bark. Three failed saves turn the target into a tree (Petrified).","GHPG24",["Druid"]],["Arcane Aegis",1,"Abjuration",["Wizard"],"Action","Self","S, M","1 minute",0,0,"","You gain 2d10 Temporary Hit Points. Melee attackers who hit you take Force damage equal to the Temporary Hit Points they remove. +2d10 per slot level above 1.","GHPG24",["Wizard"]],["Assisted Aim",1,"Enchantment",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Paladin","Ranger"],"Action","30 ft","V, S","1 minute",0,0,"","Up to 3 creatures within 30 ft get +1 to Ranged weapon attack rolls and double weapon range for 1 minute. +1 target per slot level above 1.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Paladin","Ranger"]],["Binding Pledge",1,"Divination",["Bard","Cleric","Wizard"],"1 minute","Touch","V, S, M","10 days",0,1,"","Ritual. Know at once when a willing creature breaks its promise, oath or contract, then track its distance and direction. 10 days.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Wizard"]],["Bloat",2,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Druid","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","30 ft","V, S, M","1 round",0,0,"CON","Range 30 ft. Constitution save, 3d10 Necrotic (half on success). Damage equal to or above its Constitution score makes the target float 5 ft.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Druid","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Blood Bond",3,"Enchantment",["Druid"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","1 hour",0,0,"","Spend 3 Hit Point Dice. Target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the roll, and you share a telepathic link and sense of direction for 1 hour.","GHPG24",["Druid"]],["Blood Rush",1,"Transmutation",["Druid","Ranger"],"Bonus Action","Self","S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Bonus Action, spend 1 Hit Point Die. Roll it twice and regain that total plus your spellcasting modifier in Hit Points. +1 die per slot level above 1.","GHPG24",["Druid","Ranger"]],["Blood Tide",6,"Conjuration",["Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"DEX","Spend 6 Hit Point Dice. 100 ft by 10 ft Line, Dexterity save. Fail: pushed 100 ft, Prone, Bludgeoning damage equal to a roll of the spent dice plus your modifier. Half on success.","GHPG24",["Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Blood Wisp",2,"Evocation",["Bard","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","1 hour",0,0,"","Spend 2 Hit Point Dice. A red wisp circles you and lets you reroll one damage die on your spells, but it takes that damage. 1 hour.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Bloodbane Rune",1,"Transmutation",["Cleric"],"Action","Touch","S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Spend 1 Hit Point Die. Weapon glows near Undead (30 ft) and once per turn deals extra Radiant damage equal to a roll of the spent dice. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Cleric"]],["Bloodletter",2,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Paladin","Ranger"],"Bonus Action","Touch","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Bonus Action. Nonmagical weapon: the first creature hit makes a Constitution save or gets a festering wound taking 2d6 Necrotic at the start of each turn. +1d6 per slot level above 2.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Paladin","Ranger"]],["Boil Blood",1,"Transmutation",["Cleric","Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock"],"Action","Touch","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Spend 1 Hit Point Die. A willing target takes Fire damage equal to a roll of the spent die, and its Poisoned condition ends.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock"]],["Burst Forth",7,"Conjuration",["Bard","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","200 ft","V","Instantaneous",0,0,"CON","Spend 7 Hit Point Dice. Range 200 ft. Teleport inside a creature and burst out. Constitution save, Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the spent dice plus your modifier (half on success).","GHPG24",["Bard","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Call the Rabid Beast",3,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Ranger","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"WIS","Touch. Target gets 20 Temporary Hit Points, AC 17 minimum, +5 Strength damage, a 1d6 Bite, Frightened immunity. DC 10 Wisdom save each turn or it loses control.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Ranger","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Calling Card",0,"Illusion",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"","Cantrip. Touch a corpse to leave a visible or Invisible magical mark. Anyone who takes the Study action on the corpse finds it automatically. Lasts until dispelled.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Chains of Beleth",6,"Conjuration",["Cleric","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","100 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","Range 100 ft. 20-ft Sphere of barbed chains. Dexterity save: 8d6 Piercing and Restrained. Restrained creatures take 3d6 Bludgeoning at turn end. +1d6 per slot level above 6.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Circle of Scarlet",4,"Evocation",["Sorcerer","Warlock"],"Action","120 ft","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"CON","Spend 4 Hit Point Dice. Range 120 ft. 20-ft radius, 100-ft high Cylinder. Constitution save, Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the spent dice plus your modifier (half on success). You gain 10 Temporary Hit Points per creature that fails.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer","Warlock"]],["Conjure Plants",3,"Conjuration",["Druid","Ranger","Warlock"],"Action","60 ft","V, S","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"DEX","Range 60 ft. A Large mass of vines (10 minutes) that shields you and can move 30 ft. Creatures near it make a Dexterity save or take 3d6 Slashing. +1d6 per slot level above 3.","GHPG24",["Druid","Ranger","Warlock"]],["Consume Mind",4,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","1 hour",0,0,"","Eat the brain of a creature dead 3 days or less to recall its memories for 1 hour. Recall with a Magic action and a spellcasting check against DC equal to its Intelligence score.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Consumption",1,"Evocation",["Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Spend 1 Hit Point Die. Range 60 ft. Target takes Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the spent die and repeats it on each failed Constitution save at turn end. +1 target per slot level above 1.","GHPG24",["Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Creeping Death",8,"Necromancy",["Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Spend 8 Hit Point Dice. Range 60 ft. Target dies if its Hit Points fall to or below a threshold set by your roll. Raise the threshold with Constitution saves. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Warlock","Wizard"]],["Creeping Touch",1,"Transmutation",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"","Detach your hand as a Spider for 10 minutes. Telepathy within 100 ft and see through its eyes with a Magic action. If it dies or fails to return, you take 1d6 Psychic damage.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Crimson Lash",1,"Conjuration",["Warlock","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","Self","S","1 minute",0,0,"","Spend 1 Hit Point Die. Blood lash is a Simple weapon (Light, Finesse, Reach), uses your spellcasting modifier, deals Necrotic damage of the spent die size, and lowers Hit Point maximum by the damage dealt. 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Warlock","Wizard"]],["Crown of Radiance",6,"Evocation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid"],"Action","Self","V, S","10 minutes",0,0,"","Self, 10 minutes. A Fiend, Fey or Undead within 30 ft of you takes 2d8 Radiant damage when it moves there or starts its turn there. Sheds Bright Light 30 ft, Dim Light 30 ft more.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid"]],["Curse of Conceited Obsession",6,"Enchantment",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"CHA","Level 6 staged curse. Charisma save: 8d10 Psychic and cursed on a fail, 4d6 on a success. Stages bring self-admiration, Advantage against the target, then Disadvantage on attacks. Ends as a Weeping Willow.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Crushing Sensation",6,"Enchantment",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"CON","Level 6 staged curse. Constitution save: 8d10 Thunder and cursed on a fail, 4d6 on a success. Stages bring sensory aversion, Thunder Vulnerability and no armor, then Vulnerability to all damage but Psychic outside a lair. Ends as a Sightless Agony.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Damned Aging",4,"Necromancy",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"CON","Level 4 staged curse. Strength save: 6d10 Necrotic and cursed on a fail, 2d10 on a success. Stages bring lethargy, only 25 percent of Hit Point Dice usable on a Short Rest, then Disadvantage on Strength, Dexterity and Constitution saves. Ends as a Body Snatcher.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Fastidious Pride",3,"Enchantment",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"INT","Level 3 staged curse. Intelligence save: 4d10 Psychic, Blinded 1 minute and cursed on a fail, 2d10 on a success. Stages bring paranoia, no Short Rest benefit, then Disadvantage after a failed D20 Test. Ends as a Mind Siphon.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Foul Blight",4,"Necromancy",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"CHA","Level 4 staged curse. Charisma save: 6d10 Necrotic and cursed on a fail, 3d10 and no healing for 1 minute on a success. Stages bring coughing, a rotting 10-ft aura and no Concentration, then healing only from Short Rest Hit Point Dice. Ends as a Plague Carrion.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Ill-Fated Fortune",5,"Divination",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"DEX","Level 5 staged curse. Dexterity save: 7d10 Thunder and cursed on a fail, 3d10 and Disadvantage on its first D20 Test within 1 minute on a success. Stages bring bad luck, Dexterity Disadvantage, then Disadvantage on Initiative, Speed 10 ft and Prone on a missed attack. Ends as a Herald of Calamity.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Insatiable Greed",5,"Enchantment",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"WIS","Level 5 staged curse. Wisdom save: 6d10 Cold and Speed 0 (rising 5 ft per turn) on a fail, 4d10 on a success. Stages bring trinket stealing, Wisdom Disadvantage and a hoard, then no Reactions. Ends as a Verminous Abomination.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Lost Sentiment",4,"Enchantment",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"INT","Level 4 staged curse. Intelligence save: 6d10 Force, Stunned until the end of its next turn and cursed on a fail, 3d10 and Incapacitated on a success. Stages bring forgetting, Intelligence Disadvantage, then no Bonus Actions. Ends as a Dream Whisperer.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Ravenous Hunger",3,"Enchantment",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"CON","Level 3 staged curse. Constitution save: 4d10 Poison, Poisoned 1 minute and cursed on a fail, 2d10 and Poisoned until the end of its next turn on a success. Stages bring hunger, Constitution Disadvantage and lower Hit Point maximum, then no Advantage on D20 Tests. Ends as a Bloated Gastromorph.","GHPG24",[]],["Curse of Uncontrollable Wrath",6,"Enchantment",[],"1 hour","Unlimited","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"WIS","Level 6 staged curse. Wisdom save: 8d10 Psychic and cursed on a fail, 4d10 and Disadvantage on Reaction attacks for 1 minute on a success. Stages bring aggression, no Short Rest benefit, then no Long Rest benefit. Ends as an Avatar of Slaughter.","GHPG24",[]],["Dark Sacrament",4,"Evocation",["Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Spend 4 Hit Point Dice. Melee spell attack with the dagger: spent dice plus 4d8 Necrotic. A kill grants a 10-minute dark blessing: Unassailable, Unbreakable or Unerring. +1d8 per slot level above 4.","GHPG24",["Warlock","Wizard"]],["Dazing Blast",2,"Evocation",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"CON","Range 60 ft. Constitution save: 2d6 Force and Stunned until the end of its next turn. On a success, damage only. +1 target per slot level above 2.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Earth Worm",6,"Transmutation",["Druid","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","Range 60 ft. A worm maw lasts 1 minute. Bonus Action melee spell attack: 3d8 plus your modifier Piercing. Large or smaller targets make a Dexterity save or are swallowed (Blinded, Restrained, 6d6 Bludgeoning each of your turns).","GHPG24",["Druid","Wizard"]],["Elemental Exhalation",3,"Evocation",["Druid","Sorcerer"],"Action","Self","S","Instantaneous",0,0,"DEX","Self (30-ft Cone). Choose Air, Coldfire, Earth, Fire or Water. Dexterity save: 5d6 damage of that type (half on success) plus a rider on a fail. +1d6 per slot level above 3.","GHPG24",["Druid","Sorcerer"]],["Emmeline's Essence Infusion",3,"Transmutation",["Wizard"],"8 hours","Touch","V, S, M","Special",0,0,"","Touch. Consume a vial with 1+ ounce of blood worth 100+ GP. A nonmagical weapon becomes a magic weapon needing attunement, with a bonus set by the blood: Aberration, Celestial, Dragon, Fey or Fiend. Permanent after 1 year of attunement.","GHPG24",["Wizard"]],["Enspelled Armament",2,"Conjuration",["Sorcerer"],"Bonus Action","Self","M","1 hour",0,0,"","Self, 1 hour. Create an energy replica of a Simple or Martial weapon you are proficient with. Use your spellcasting modifier, no ammunition, thrown weapons return, damage becomes Force. +1d4 per slot level above 2.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer"]],["Extract Iron",3,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Wizard"],"1 minute","Self","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Spend 3 Hit Point Dice. Draw pounds of iron from your blood equal to the roll and shape nonmagical metal objects of poor but working quality. More dice and iron per slot level above 3.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Wizard"]],["Fiend Flesh",2,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Touch. A willing creature gains red scales for 1 hour: Resistance to Cold, Fire and Lightning, Immunity to Poison damage. Concentration.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Flash Fever",3,"Necromancy",["Druid","Warlock"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Range 60 ft. Constitution save: 4d6 Fire on a fail, spell ends on a success. Then 2d6 Fire at the start of each turn. Three successful saves end it, three failures deal 8d6 Fire. +1d6 initial per slot level above 3.","GHPG24",["Druid","Warlock"]],["Flense",8,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Range 60 ft. Ranged spell attack: 8d6 Necrotic on a hit, with a Constitution save for half. Each turn, a Magic action forces another save for 8d6 (half on success). Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Wizard"]],["Fleshcrawl",7,"Necromancy",["Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","100 ft","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Range 100 ft. Constitution save: 8d10 Necrotic (half on success). The flayed skin rises as an allied Fleshling Construct that shares your Initiative and acts right after you. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Warlock","Wizard"]],["Frightful Start",0,"Illusion",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","30 ft","V, S, M","1 round",0,0,"WIS","Cantrip. Range 30 ft. The target succeeds on a Wisdom save or has the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Ghost Light",1,"Evocation",["Bard","Cleric","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","1 hour",0,0,"","Touch an object up to 10 ft across. It sheds silvery Bright Light in 20 ft and Dim Light 20 ft more, visible only to creatures you named within 10 ft. 1 hour.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Greater Animate Dead",5,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Wizard"],"1 minute","10 ft","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Range 10 ft. Raise up to 5 Undead of CR 2 or lower from corpses. Command them as a Bonus Action within 120 ft. Control lasts 24 hours and can be renewed on up to four creatures. +1 Undead per slot level above 5.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Wizard"]],["Heartseeker",6,"Evocation",["Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","300 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Spend 6 Hit Point Dice. Range 300 ft. Ranged spell attack: Piercing damage equal to a roll of the spent dice. The first hit on the target each round after its turn is a Critical Hit. Constitution save each turn end, 3d8 Necrotic on success ends it. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Holy Word",0,"Evocation",["Cleric"],"Action","60 ft","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Cantrip. Range 60 ft. Ranged spell attack: 1d8 Radiant. Fey, Fiend or Undead also lose 10 ft of Speed and cannot take Reactions until the end of their next turn. Damage 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at 11, 4d8 at 17.","GHPG24",["Cleric"]],["Hunter Sense",0,"Divination",["Druid"],"Action","Touch","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Cantrip. Touch a willing creature. For 1 minute, when it makes a Wisdom (Perception) check, a d20 roll of 9 or lower counts as 10. Concentration.","GHPG24",["Druid"]],["Illusory Instrument",0,"Illusion",["Bard","Warlock"],"Action","Touch","V, S","10 minutes",0,0,"","Conjure a weightless illusory copy of an instrument for 10 minutes. A Bonus Action triggers sound effects, a beat, or recordings.","GHPG24",["Bard","Warlock"]],["Incite Riot",5,"Enchantment",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","30 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"WIS","Wisdom save or creatures within 30 ft are Charmed and attack the nearest foe. Repeat the save each turn. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Intaglio",1,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Paladin","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,1,"","Copy one page of non-magical text or art per Magic action onto a medium you supply. Halves spellbook copy time and cost. Concentration, 1 hour.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Paladin","Wizard"]],["Investiture of Venom",5,"Transmutation",["Druid","Ranger"],"Action","Self","V, S","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"CON","10 minutes: Poison immunity, see who resists Poison, strip a creature's Poison defenses, or blast a 15-ft Line for 4d6 Poison. Concentration.","GHPG24",["Druid","Ranger"]],["Life Tether",2,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","120 ft","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"WIS","Wisdom save: a tether makes the target take half of any damage you take, as Necrotic. Concentration, 1 minute. More tethers at higher slots.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Lifesink",8,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Self (15 ft emanation)","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","15-ft Emanation: others that enter or start there take 4d6 Necrotic, and you regain 4d6 HP plus 1 per creature in it each turn. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Little Death",5,"Necromancy",["Warlock"],"Action","Self","S, M","8 hours",0,0,"","You die and rise as a Ghost for 1d8 hours (rolled secretly by the GM), then return to life with half your HP maximum if your token is on your corpse. Up to 8 hours.","GHPG24",["Warlock"]],["Maelfa's Quickened Class",3,"Enchantment",["Wizard"],"10 minutes","30 ft","V, S","24 hours",0,0,"","10-minute lecture: 10 willing creatures within 30 ft gain a spell, a skill proficiency, or a language you know for 24 hours.","GHPG24",["Wizard"]],["Magic Mirror",5,"Abjuration",["Sorcerer"],"Reaction","Self","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Reaction: redirect a spell that targets you to a creature you see within 60 ft. Level 6+ spells need an ability check.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer"]],["Melting Curse",6,"Transmutation",["Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","100 ft","V, S, M","1 minute",0,0,"DEX","Dexterity save: 5d8 Fire and a held or worn metal object melts. Touching the puddle again costs another 5d8 Fire. 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Mirror Spell",3,"Abjuration",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Reaction","60 ft","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Reaction: copy and cast a spell of level 3 or lower that you see someone cast, without a slot or components. Level 3+ needs a check.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Mortality",5,"Transmutation",["Sorcerer"],"Action","120 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CHA","Spend five Hit Point Dice. Charisma save or a planar creature loses that many HP (and HP maximum) and becomes a mortal Humanoid. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer"]],["Neutralize Aura",1,"Abjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Paladin"],"1 minute","Touch","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","A willing creature cannot be perceived by Fey, Fiends, Celestials and Undead for 1 hour. Ends if it attacks, deals damage, casts, or gets within 5 ft of them. Concentration.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Paladin"]],["Overgrow",2,"Transmutation",["Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"STR","Vines pin a creature (Strength save or Restrained) or fix an object in place. Huge or smaller, 60 ft. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer"]],["Perfection",9,"Abjuration",["Bard","Cleric"],"Action","60 ft","V","1 minute",0,0,"","Remake a creature in an Arch Seraph's image: cure Poisoned, suppress curses, full HP, low ability scores become 18, plus one of six blessings. 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric"]],["Phoenix Flames",9,"Evocation",["Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer"],"Action","Self (30 ft emanation)","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"CON","You burn up and die in a 30-ft Emanation of holy fire. Constitution save: 30d6 Radiant and 1 Exhaustion, half on a save. You rise after 10 minutes.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer"]],["Power Word Maim",7,"Enchantment",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V","Instantaneous",0,0,"CON","Target with 125 HP or fewer takes 8d10 Necrotic and is Prone. Otherwise its Speed is 0 until it saves (Constitution) at a turn end.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Preserve",0,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","12 hours",0,0,"","Food and perishables up to 5 lb in a sack do not age or decay for 12 hours.","GHPG24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Primordial Power",4,"Transmutation",["Druid"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","A touched creature speaks Primordial and gains an elemental boon of your choice (Air, Coldfire, Earth, Fire or Water). Concentration, 1 hour.","GHPG24",["Druid"]],["Reanimate",3,"Evocation",["Druid"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Spend three Hit Point Dice to revive a creature dead for under 10 minutes with 1 HP and temporary HP, a +2 bonus to D20 Tests, then Exhaustion.","GHPG24",["Druid"]],["Red Rain",8,"Conjuration",["Cleric","Warlock"],"10 minutes","Self","V, S, M","Up to 8 hours",1,0,"WIS","Spend eight Hit Point Dice. Blood rain over 5 miles frightens Beasts and Plants and drains exposed creatures with Exhaustion and 2d10 Necrotic per 10 minutes. 8 hours, Concentration.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Warlock"]],["Ride the Lightning",4,"Conjuration",["Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"DEX","Become lightning along a 5-ft-wide Line up to 60 ft and reappear at the far end. Dexterity save: 4d6 Lightning, half on a save.","GHPG24",["Druid","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Sanguine Fusillade",7,"Evocation",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Spend seven Hit Point Dice. Target takes Piercing damage equal to the roll, then seven darts burst out. Each dart is a ranged spell attack within 60 ft.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Sanguine Poppet",3,"Transmutation",["Bard","Warlock"],"1 minute","Touch","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"DEX","1 minute cast, spend three Hit Point Dice. A poppet you control (AC 10 + Prof + casting mod, 30 HP) that you can see through and detonate. Concentration, 1 hour.","GHPG24",["Bard","Warlock"]],["Sanguine Shield",2,"Abjuration",["Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Spend two Hit Point Dice. Gain 5 Temporary HP per wounded creature within 30 ft (max 15) and Cover while you have them. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Seal Spellcasting",2,"Abjuration",["Sorcerer"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"CHA","Charisma save when the target casts: on a fail the slot is spent and the spell does nothing, on a success it takes 3d8 Force. Ends after the save. Concentration, 10 minutes.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer"]],["Sense Lifeblood",2,"Divination",["Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer"],"Bonus Action","Self","S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Bonus Action, spend two Hit Point Dice. Sense blood kin and the health state of creatures you see, and add Necrotic damage to hits on Bloodied foes. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer"]],["Serpent Tongue",3,"Transmutation",["Warlock","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","Self","V, S","1 minute",0,0,"","Bonus Action melee spell attack within 10 ft: 1d12 Piercing and Poisoned for the duration. 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Warlock","Wizard"]],["Shared Judgement",4,"Evocation",["Cleric"],"Bonus Action","Self","V","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Once per turn when you drop an Undead to 0 HP, deal 5d6 Radiant to a creature you see within 60 ft. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Cleric"]],["Shroud Blood",1,"Illusion",["Bard","Druid","Ranger","Wizard"],"Action","30 ft","V, S","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"","Spend one Hit Point Die. A creature gets Advantage on Stealth checks and can regain Invisibility as a Reaction for rounds equal to dice spent. Concentration, 10 minutes.","GHPG24",["Bard","Druid","Ranger","Wizard"]],["Somnolence",1,"Enchantment",["Bard","Warlock"],"Action","30 ft","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Spend one Hit Point Die. Roll it plus 2d12. If the total meets a creature's current HP it sleeps 1 minute, or 24 hours if it meets its HP maximum.","GHPG24",["Bard","Warlock"]],["Spirit Swarm",5,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Wizard"],"Action","120 ft","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CHA","Charisma save: 8d8 Psychic and Frightened (half damage on a save). The target needs Charisma 3 or higher. 120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Wizard"]],["Splattering Smite",5,"Abjuration",["Paladin"],"Reaction","Self","V","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Reaction, spend five Hit Point Dice. Once per turn when you hit with a Melee weapon or Unarmed Strike, regain HP equal to a roll of one die spent. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Paladin"]],["Steal Immortality",9,"Transmutation",["Warlock"],"Reaction","300 ft","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Reaction, spend nine Hit Point Dice. Gain twice the roll as Temporary HP and take the target's creature type and its benefits, plus Poison immunity and physical Resistance.","GHPG24",["Warlock"]],["Suffocate",3,"Conjuration",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Ranged spell attack: force hands Restrain a creature within 60 ft, which cannot breathe and gains Exhaustion once out of breath. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Summon Plant (Grim Hollow)",2,"Conjuration",["Druid","Ranger"],"Action","90 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Call a Plant Spirit ally with a Blooming, Oaken or Thorny feature. It acts right after you and lasts up to 1 hour. Concentration.","GHPG24",["Druid","Ranger"]],["Summon Sea Spirit",3,"Conjuration",["Druid","Warlock"],"Action","90 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Call a Sea Serpent Spirit ally with an Enormous Mouth, Glowing Lantern or Scaled Wings feature. It acts right after you and lasts up to 1 hour. Concentration.","GHPG24",["Druid","Warlock"]],["Supernal Smite",4,"Evocation",["Paladin"],"Bonus Action","Self","V","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Bonus Action on a hit: extra 4d6 Force, breaks Concentration, and ends ongoing spells of level 3 or lower on the target (checks for level 4+).","GHPG24",["Paladin"]],["Theft of Vitae",2,"Transmutation",["Druid","Wizard"],"Reaction","Self","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Reaction: the triggering creature takes Necrotic damage equal to a Hit Point Die roll, and you gain Temporary HP equal to that plus the triggering damage (max 15).","GHPG24",["Druid","Wizard"]],["Thorn Armor",1,"Abjuration",["Druid","Ranger"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","10 minutes",0,0,"","A willing creature gains 3d6 Temporary HP. Melee attackers take Piercing damage equal to the Temporary HP they remove. 10 minutes.","GHPG24",["Druid","Ranger"]],["Tremor",1,"Evocation",["Bard","Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Self (15 ft emanation)","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","15-ft Emanation of shaking ground: Difficult Terrain, Dexterity save or 1d6 Bludgeoning and Prone, once per turn per creature. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Bard","Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Undead Enthrallment",8,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Warlock","Wizard"],"1 hour","10 ft","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","1 hour cast. Raise corpses as Undead of CR 3 or lower under your command for 24 hours. Recast to keep control. Up to four controlled.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Vampiric Claws",1,"Transmutation",["Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","Self","V","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Bonus Action: claws make your Unarmed Strike deal 1d6 Slashing using your spellcasting modifier, and each hit grants Temporary HP equal to that modifier. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Druid","Ranger","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Vibrating Humors",1,"Evocation",["Bard","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","30 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Spend one Hit Point Die. Constitution save or Thunder damage equal to the roll and Disadvantage on Stealth, repeating each turn. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Viscous Sheath",4,"Necromancy",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","10 minutes",0,0,"STR","Spend seven Hit Point Dice. Melee attackers take Necrotic damage equal to a die roll plus your casting modifier, and you can trap their weapons. 10 minutes.","GHPG24",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Wall of Gloom",8,"Conjuration",["Bard","Wizard"],"Action","120 ft","V, S, M","10 minutes",0,0,"CHA","Wall of grief-energy up to 60 ft long or a 20-ft-diameter ring, blocks sight, Charisma saves for Incapacitated nearby and Exhaustion inside. 10 minutes.","GHPG24",["Bard","Wizard"]],["Weave Numen",6,"Divination",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"","Sense magic within 120 ft and gain 13 threads to boost your spells, interrupt enemy spells, or add 4 damage or healing per thread. Concentration, 10 minutes.","GHPG24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Wilting Smite",2,"Transmutation",["Paladin"],"Bonus Action","Self","V","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Bonus Action, spend two Hit Point Dice. The creature you hit loses all damage Resistances until your next turn and takes extra Necrotic damage.","GHPG24",["Paladin"]],["Wipe Face",9,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"CON","Curse a creature within 60 ft: its face smooths over, leaving it Blinded, Incapacitated and suffocating. Constitution save each turn to end it. Concentration, 10 minutes.","GHPG24",["Cleric","Wizard"]],["Wrack",2,"Necromancy",["Cleric"],"Action","30 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Constitution save or the target's Speed is halved and it has Disadvantage on attack rolls. Repeat the save each turn. Concentration, 1 minute.","GHPG24",["Cleric"]]];
var SPF={"Arboreal Curse":"Range 60 ft. You try to turn one creature you can see into wood. The target makes a Constitution save. On a fail it has the Restrained condition as bark spreads over its flesh. On a success its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn.\n\n**Repeating saves.** A creature Restrained by this spell makes a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns. Three successes end the condition. Three failures turn it into a tree and it has the Petrified condition. The saves need not be consecutive. Keep a separate count of successes and failures until one count reaches three.\n\n**Lasting harm.** If the creature is burned, chopped down or otherwise destroyed while Petrified, it dies. The change lasts until reversed within 1 year by Greater Restoration, Wish or similar magic. If the creature stays a tree for 1 year and 1 day, the change becomes permanent and nothing can restore its original form.","Arcane Aegis":"Self, 1 minute. A shimmering light surrounds you, then fades. You gain 2d10 Temporary Hit Points. If a creature hits you with a melee attack before the spell ends, it takes Force damage equal to the number of Temporary Hit Points that attack removed from you. The spell ends early when you have no Temporary Hit Points left.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You gain an extra 2d10 Temporary Hit Points for each slot level above 1.","Assisted Aim":"Range 30 ft, 1 minute. You sharpen the aim of up to three creatures within range. Each target gains a +1 bonus to attack rolls made with Ranged weapons. The normal and long range of Ranged weapons a target wields are also doubled for the duration.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 1.","Binding Pledge":"Touch, 10 days, ritual. A willing creature within range makes a promise, swears an oath or enters a contract. For the duration you know at once if it breaks that promise, oath or contract. When that happens, you know the creature's distance and direction for the rest of the duration. If the spell is dispelled, you know it immediately but do not learn the creature's distance and direction.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 3 or 4 slot the duration is 30 days. With a level 5 or 6 slot it is 1 year. With a level 7 or higher slot it lasts until dispelled.","Bloat":"Range 30 ft, 1 round. You make the gases inside a creature you can see swell. The target makes a Constitution save and takes 3d10 Necrotic damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Floating.** If the damage the creature takes equals or exceeds its Constitution score, it floats 5 feet straight up and stays suspended until the start of your next turn. It can only move by pushing or pulling on a fixed object or surface within reach, such as a wall or ceiling, and moves as if climbing. When the spell ends, it drifts gently to the ground.","Blood Bond":"Touch, 1 hour. To cast this spell you must expend three Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Roll the expended dice. The target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the total.\n\n**Link.** For the duration you know the target's direction and distance, and you and the target can speak telepathically. You can also target that creature with a spell that has a range of Self or Touch, no matter the distance between you. These benefits are suppressed while you are on different planes.\n\n**Breaking the bond.** The target can end the spell early at any time. If it does, it loses any remaining Temporary Hit Points from this spell and takes Necrotic damage equal to the Temporary Hit Points lost.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 5 or 6 slot the duration is 8 hours. With a level 7 or 8 slot it is 24 hours. With a level 9 slot it is 7 days.","Blood Rush":"Self, Bonus Action. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. Roll that Hit Point Die twice and add the results. You regain Hit Points equal to that total plus your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 1.","Blood Tide":"Self (100-foot Line), Action. To cast this spell you must expend six Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. A gout of blood blasts out from you in a Line 100 feet long and 10 feet wide, in a direction you choose. Each creature in the Line makes a Dexterity save.\n\n**Failed save.** The creature is pushed 100 feet along the Line away from you, has the Prone condition, and takes Bludgeoning damage equal to a roll of the Hit Point Dice you expended plus your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Successful save.** The creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 6.","Blood Wisp":"Self, 1 hour. Material cost: a ruby worth 10 GP. To cast this spell you must expend two Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Roll the expended dice. You create a red wisp whose Hit Points equal the roll plus your spellcasting ability modifier. It circles your head, has an AC of 10 plus your spellcasting ability modifier, and uses your saving throws.\n\n**Rerolls.** Each time you roll damage for a spell while the wisp circles you, you can reroll one of the damage dice. You must use the new roll, and the wisp takes damage equal to that new roll. If the wisp drops to 0 Hit Points, the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 2.","Bloodbane Rune":"Touch, Concentration up to 1 minute. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. You draw a rune in blood on a weapon of your choice within range. While you wield it for the duration, the weapon weeps a phantasmal red ichor whenever it is within 30 feet of an Undead creature. Once per turn, when you damage an Undead creature with the weapon, you deal extra Radiant damage. Roll the number of Hit Point Dice you expended to cast the spell to find that damage.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 1. With a level 2 slot, Concentration can last up to 10 minutes. With a level 3 or higher slot, up to 1 hour.","Bloodletter":"Touch, Bonus Action, Concentration up to 1 minute. You touch a nonmagical weapon. Until the spell ends, the first creature the weapon hits must succeed on a Constitution save or gain a festering wound. A creature with a festering wound takes 2d6 Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns for the duration. A creature can have only one festering wound at a time. If the creature receives healing, the spell and the recurring damage end.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 2.","Boil Blood":"Touch. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. A willing target takes Fire damage equal to a roll of the expended Hit Point Die. If the target has the Poisoned condition, that condition ends at once.","Burst Forth":"Range 200 ft. To cast this spell you must expend seven Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. You teleport inside a creature you can see within range and burst out of it in a spray of gore, landing in the nearest unoccupied space. The target makes a Constitution save. It takes Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the Hit Point Dice you expended plus your spellcasting ability modifier on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 7.","Call the Rabid Beast":"Touch, Concentration up to 1 minute. A creature you touch becomes a rabid monster full of primal fury. It grows thick fur and a fanged maw, and gains 20 Temporary Hit Points. While transformed it has these effects:\n- Its AC is 17 if its AC is lower than that.\n- It gets a +5 bonus to damage rolls with Strength-based attacks.\n- It can make a Bite attack as a Bonus Action. The Bite deals 1d6 plus its Strength modifier Slashing damage.\n- It is immune to the Frightened condition.\n- It cannot cast spells or maintain Concentration.\n\n**Loss of control.** At the start of each of its turns, the creature must succeed on a DC 10 Wisdom save or lose control until the spell ends. A creature that has lost control must take the Attack action on each of its turns, using melee attacks against the nearest creature. If none is within reach, it must use its movement, and the Dash action if needed, to move toward the nearest creature.","Calling Card":"Touch, until dispelled. You touch a corpse and leave a magical mark on it. You choose whether the mark is visible, appearing as a rune or word written on the flesh, or Invisible. A creature that takes the Study action to examine the corpse specifically detects the mark automatically, whether it is visible or Invisible.","Chains of Beleth":"Range 100 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. Barbed chains ending in meat hooks burst from the ground at a point you can see within range and flail about in a Sphere of 20-foot radius centered there. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 8d6 Piercing damage and has the Restrained condition until the spell ends.\n\n**Entering the area.** The first time a creature enters the area on a turn, or starts its turn there, it must succeed on a Dexterity save or have the Restrained condition while in the area or until it breaks free.\n\n**Breaking free.** A creature Restrained by the chains can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. On a success it is no longer Restrained.\n\n**Ongoing damage.** When a creature Restrained by this spell ends its turn, it takes 3d6 Bludgeoning damage.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The initial and later damage both increase by 1d6 for each slot level above 6.","Circle of Scarlet":"Range 120 ft. To cast this spell you must expend four Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. A crimson pillar erupts from the ground in a Cylinder of 20-foot radius and 100-foot height centered on a point within range. Each creature in the Cylinder makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the Hit Point Dice you expended plus your spellcasting ability modifier. On a success it takes half as much.\n\n**Feeding.** For each creature that fails the save, you gain 10 Temporary Hit Points.","Conjure Plants":"Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 10 minutes. You conjure a Large mass of animated vines, stems, shoots, roots and leaves in an unoccupied space you can see within range. It lasts for the duration.\n\n**Cover.** While you are within 5 feet of the plants or share a space with them, you count as being in a Lightly Obscured area. Other creatures cannot enter the plants' space.\n\n**Moving.** When you move on your turn, you can also move the plants up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.\n\n**Lashing out.** Whenever the plants move within 5 feet of a creature you can see, or a creature you can see enters a space within 5 feet of them or ends its turn there, you can force that creature to make a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 3d6 Slashing damage. A creature makes this save only once per turn.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3.","Consume Mind":"Self, 1 hour. Material: a 1-ounce piece of fresh or magically preserved brain from another creature. You consume the brain of a dead creature and gain access to its memories. The creature must have a brain and cannot be Undead. The spell fails if the creature has been dead and unpreserved for more than 3 days.\n\n**Recalling.** Until the spell ends, you can try to recall a memory, such as family history, recent events, building layouts, passwords or details of the creature's death. To do so, take a Magic action and make an ability check using your spellcasting ability modifier. The DC equals the corpse's Intelligence score. After you take a Magic action to recall a piece of information, you cannot try to recall that same piece again.","Consumption":"Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. Choose a creature within range and roll the expended die. The target takes Necrotic damage equal to the result. At the end of each of its turns while the spell lasts, the target makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes that damage again. On a success the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 1.","Creeping Death":"Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. To cast this spell you must expend eight Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Roll the expended dice. The total is the target's Creeping Death threshold. For the duration, if the creature's Hit Points are reduced to its Creeping Death threshold or lower, it dies at once.\n\n**Pushing the threshold.** As a Bonus Action, you can force the target to make a Constitution save. On a fail, roll 2d6 and add the result to the threshold. On a success, add half the result instead. If the creature succeeds on three of these saves, which need not be consecutive, the spell ends early.","Creeping Touch":"Self, Concentration up to 10 minutes. You detach your hand at the wrist and turn it into a Spider. While the spider is within 100 feet of you, you can speak with it telepathically. As a Magic action you can see through its eyes and hear what it hears until the start of your next turn. During that time you are unaware of your own surroundings.\n\n**Ending.** As a Bonus Action you can command the spider to return to you. When it arrives, it reattaches as your hand and the spell ends. If the spider is killed or does not return before the spell ends, your hand is restored but you take 1d6 Psychic damage.","Crimson Lash":"Self, 1 minute. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. A writhing lash of coagulated blood springs from your hand. It has these properties:\n- It counts as a Simple weapon and you are proficient with it.\n- It has the Light, Finesse and Reach properties.\n- You can use your spellcasting ability modifier instead of Strength or Dexterity for attack and damage rolls with it.\n- Its damage die matches the Hit Point Die you expended, and its damage is Necrotic.\n- Each time a creature takes damage from the lash, its Hit Point maximum decreases by the damage taken.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 3 or 4 slot, you can make two attacks with the lash when you take the Attack action. With a level 5 or higher slot, you can make three.","Crown of Radiance":"Self, 10 minutes. A flaming crown of holy light settles on your head until the spell ends. A Fiend, Fey or Undead that moves within 30 feet of you, or starts its turn within 30 feet of you, takes 2d8 Radiant damage. The crown sheds Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for another 30 feet.","Curse of Conceited Obsession":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a thread from the target's bed or clothes, a handful of teeth and a gilded mirror worth 1,000+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with obsessive self-infatuation. The target makes a Charisma save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 4d6 Psychic damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it also takes 1d6 Psychic damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 8d10 Psychic damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the cursed creature looks into a mirror or reflective surface, the surface cracks or warps and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It must stop and admire itself whenever it sees its reflection and fusses constantly over its looks.\n\n**Stage 2.** It becomes obsessed with finding its reflection everywhere, even in foes' eyes. Attacks against it have Advantage.\n\n**Stage 3.** It feels driven to find or build a place where it can see itself from many angles, and it must stay there admiring itself. It also has Disadvantage on attack rolls.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Weeping Willow.","Curse of Crushing Sensation":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a drop of the target's blood, a shred of silk and a horn worth 1,000+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with painful hypersensitivity. The target makes a Constitution save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 4d6 Thunder damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it also takes 1d6 Thunder damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 8d10 Thunder damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target hears a loud noise, it gets a crippling headache and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It avoids Bright Light, loud noises and extreme temperatures, and dislikes being touched.\n\n**Stage 2.** It cannot bear rough or heavy clothing and cannot wear armor. It has Vulnerability to Thunder damage. It also has Disadvantage on attack rolls if it or its target is in an area of Bright Light.\n\n**Stage 3.** Even mild sensation is intolerable. It feels driven to find a dark, quiet lair such as a deep cave or dungeon and cannot willingly leave it. While outside its lair it has Vulnerability to all damage except Psychic.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Sightless Agony.","Curse of Damned Aging":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a childhood possession of the target, a pint of blood and a watch worth 600+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with horrific aging. The target makes a Strength save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 2d10 Necrotic damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it has Vulnerability to Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing damage, chosen by you when you cast the spell.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 6d10 Necrotic damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** When the target next finishes a Long Rest, it finds new wrinkles, grey hairs or spots, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It feels compelled to rest whenever it can and becomes lethargic and lazy.\n\n**Stage 2.** It becomes feeble. After a Short Rest it can use only 25 percent of its Hit Point Dice (rounded up) to regain Hit Points.\n\n**Stage 3.** It ages rapidly and grows decrepit. It has Disadvantage on Strength, Dexterity and Constitution saves.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Body Snatcher.","Curse of Fastidious Pride":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a shred of the target's clothing, an uncrushed dead spider and a sewing needle worth 600+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with narcissistic hubris. The target makes an Intelligence save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 2d10 Psychic damage and knows it was cursed.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 4d10 Psychic damage, has the Blinded condition for 1 minute, and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target hears its name spoken, the speaker sounds derisive whatever their real tone, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It hears veiled insults everywhere and believes everyone envies its brilliance and talent.\n\n**Stage 2.** It is restless unless it is working toward a goal. It gains no benefit from a Short Rest.\n\n**Stage 3.** It believes everyone is part of a conspiracy to ruin it. Whenever it fails a D20 Test, it has Disadvantage on the next D20 Test it makes.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Mind Siphon.","Curse of Foul Blight":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a shred of the target's hair or flesh, a chunk of rotten meat and a jewelry box worth 600+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with a putrefying, stinking pox. The target makes a Charisma save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 3d10 Necrotic damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it cannot gain Temporary Hit Points or regain Hit Points.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 6d10 Necrotic damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target searches its garments or gear, it finds them infested with insects, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It has a minor cough and breaks into a coughing fit whenever it speaks more than a few words. This does not affect spellcasting.\n\n**Stage 2.** The stench of rot hangs around it. Within 10 feet of the creature, food and drink spoil quickly, jewelry tarnishes and wood rots. It has Disadvantage on Charisma checks and saves and cannot maintain Concentration.\n\n**Stage 3.** Its skin is covered in pockmarks, pustules and lesions, and insects swarm its clothes. It can regain Hit Points only by spending Hit Point Dice after a Short Rest.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Plague Carrion.","Curse of Ill-Fated Fortune":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a discarded piece of the target's gear, a splinter of bone and a set of dice worth 800+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with lethal bad luck. The target makes a Dexterity save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 3d10 Thunder damage and knows it was cursed. It has Disadvantage on the first D20 Test it makes in the next 1 minute.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 7d10 Thunder damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target walks through a doorway, it stubs its toe or bangs its head, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** Minor mishaps follow it. Shops close just as it arrives and its gear breaks at awkward moments.\n\n**Stage 2.** It becomes a beacon of bad luck, and harmless setbacks turn dangerous. Objects keep ending up in its way. It has Disadvantage on Dexterity checks and saves.\n\n**Stage 3.** It is prone to accidents, and even simple tasks have unforeseen deadly results. It has Disadvantage on Initiative checks, its Speed is reduced to 10 feet, and it has the Prone condition whenever it misses an attack roll.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Herald of Calamity.","Curse of Insatiable Greed":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a coin the target once owned, a rat's tail and a golden crown of thorns worth 800+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with bitter, self-destructive greed. The target makes a Wisdom save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 4d10 Cold damage and knows it was cursed.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 6d10 Cold damage and its Speed is reduced to 0 for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, its Speed increases by 5 feet until it reaches its normal maximum. It is also cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target finishes a Short Rest or Long Rest, it notices a valued item is missing, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It feels compelled to steal trinkets.\n\n**Stage 2.** It finds a secret place to stash stolen trinkets and grows anxious about leaving it for long. It has Disadvantage on Wisdom checks and saves.\n\n**Stage 3.** It is driven to turn its hoard into a labyrinth of possessions and treasure and wants to stay in this lair. It cannot take Reactions.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Verminous Abomination.","Curse of Lost Sentiment":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a lock of hair from someone the target loves, an animal's heart and an idol worth 600+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with lost memories and horrific madness. The target makes an Intelligence save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 3d10 Force damage and has the Incapacitated condition until the end of its next turn. It does not know it was cursed.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 6d10 Force damage, has the Stunned condition until the end of its next turn, and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target finishes a Long Rest, it has nightmares of being abandoned or left alone, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It begins forgetting events of the past few days and the names of acquaintances.\n\n**Stage 2.** It forgets everyone but its closest companions and imagines hidden threats and scheming rivals. It has Disadvantage on Intelligence checks and saves.\n\n**Stage 3.** It forgets even its closest companions, its own identity and its goals. The curse invents the delusion of a great conspiracy that only it can stop, and it feels compelled to do whatever it thinks is needed to uncover it. It cannot take Bonus Actions.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Dream Whisperer.","Curse of Ravenous Hunger":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a morsel of food that belonged to the target, a sun-dried slug and a dining plate worth 400+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with painful, unending starvation. The target makes a Constitution save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 2d10 Poison damage, has the Poisoned condition until the end of its next turn, and knows it was cursed.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 4d10 Poison damage, has the Poisoned condition for 1 minute, and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time it eats a meal, the creature bites its tongue and its mouth fills with blood, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It is gripped by an insatiable appetite.\n\n**Stage 2.** It feels compelled to eat unsuitable things such as coins, flowers, glass and dirt. It has Disadvantage on Constitution saves, and its Hit Point maximum decreases by its character level (or by its number of Hit Point Dice if it has no character level).\n\n**Stage 3.** It becomes ravenous and must eat Humanoid flesh, since no other food satisfies it. It cannot have Advantage on D20 Tests.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Bloated Gastromorph.","Curse of Uncontrollable Wrath":"Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: blood or other fluid of the target, a severed hand and a serrated knife worth 1,000+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with an uncontrollable temper and a lust for violence. The target makes a Wisdom save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 4d10 Psychic damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it has Disadvantage on attacks made with a Reaction.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 8d10 Psychic damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the cursed creature attacks with a weapon or casts a spell using a Spellcasting Focus, an old wound reopens and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It is easily agitated and aggressive.\n\n**Stage 2.** It becomes obsessed with violence. Fighting alone thrills it and its attitude to allies sours as the curse grows. It gains no benefit from a Short Rest.\n\n**Stage 3.** It is driven by insatiable bloodlust and cannot rest while enemies remain to be slaughtered. It gains no benefit from a Long Rest.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes an Avatar of Slaughter.","Dark Sacrament":"Self, Action. Material: a dagger encrusted in jewels worth 100+ GP. To cast this spell you must expend four Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Make a melee spell attack with the Material component against a creature within 5 feet. On a hit, roll the Hit Point Dice you expended plus 4d8. You deal Necrotic damage equal to the total.\n\n**Dark blessing.** If this damage reduces the creature to 0 Hit Points, it dies at once and you gain one of these dark blessings of your choice:\n- Unassailable. You have Advantage on all saving throws.\n- Unbreakable. Your size increases by one category (Medium to Large, for example). At the start of each of your turns you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d4 damage.\n- Unerring. Your Proficiency Bonus increases by 2.\n\nWhen you take Radiant damage while you have a dark blessing, you take an extra 1d4 Radiant damage. The blessing ends after 10 minutes or when you drop to 0 Hit Points, whichever comes first.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The initial damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 4.","Dazing Blast":"Range 60 ft. A wave of force leaves your palms and strikes a creature within range. The target makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 2d6 Force damage and has the Stunned condition until the end of its next turn. On a success it takes the damage only.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 2.","Earth Worm":"Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. You turn the ground at an unoccupied point within range into a wormlike maw. As a Bonus Action, make a melee spell attack against a creature within 5 feet of the worm. On a hit, the target takes Piercing damage equal to 3d8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Swallowing.** If the target is Large or smaller, it must succeed on a Dexterity save or be swallowed. A swallowed creature has the Blinded and Restrained conditions, has Cover against attacks and effects from outside the worm, and takes 6d6 Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of your turns.\n\n**Escaping.** A trapped creature can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. On a success it is spat out, has the Prone condition, and lands in an unoccupied space within 10 feet of the worm.\n\n**Moving.** As a Bonus Action, you can move the worm up to 30 feet.","Elemental Exhalation":"Self (30-foot Cone). When you cast this spell, choose one element. It sets the damage type and adds an effect on a failed save. Each creature in the Cone of destructive elemental energy makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 5d6 damage of the chosen type. On a success it takes half as much damage only.\n- Air. Thunder damage. Each creature that fails is pushed 10 feet away from you.\n- Coldfire. Cold damage. Each creature that fails has the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn.\n- Earth. Bludgeoning damage. Each creature that fails has its Speed reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn.\n- Fire. Fire damage. Each creature that fails is set alight and takes 2d6 Fire damage at the end of its next turn. As an action it can put out the flames by giving itself the Prone condition and rolling on the ground. The fire also goes out if it is doused, submerged or suffocated.\n- Water. Acid damage. Each creature that fails has the Prone condition.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3.","Emmeline's Essence Infusion":"Touch, lasts while you are attuned. Material: a diamond vial holding at least 1 ounce of blood, worth at least 100 GP, which the spell consumes. You target one nonmagical weapon within range. It becomes magical and gains a benefit based on the creature type of the blood used. The weapon requires Attunement and only the attuned creature gains the benefits.\n- Aberration. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 Psychic damage on a hit. You can also speak telepathically with any creature that has taken at least 1 damage from this weapon in the last 24 hours, if you are both on the same plane.\n- Celestial. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 Radiant damage on a hit. As a Bonus Action you can make the weapon shed Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for another 30 feet. Another Bonus Action ends the light.\n- Dragon. Your attack rolls with this weapon score a Critical Hit on a 19 or 20 on the d20. You also have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the Frightened condition.\n- Fey. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d4 Force damage on a hit. Once per turn, when you hit a creature within 30 feet with this weapon, you can teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of it.\n- Fiend. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage on a hit. As a Bonus Action you can change this extra damage to Cold or Fire.\n\n**Duration.** When you cast the spell, you attune to the weapon, and the spell lasts as long as you stay attuned. During that time the item can be affected by Dispel Magic. If you stay attuned for 1 year, the enchantment becomes permanent and the spell ends.","Enspelled Armament":"Self, 1 hour. Material: a vial of oil and water. Choose one Simple or Martial weapon. An iridescent energy copy of it appears in your hands. For the duration you are proficient with it, and when you attack with it you can use your spellcasting ability modifier for attack and damage rolls instead of Strength or Dexterity. Attacks with it need no ammunition, and if you throw it as part of a ranged attack, it returns to your hand right after the attack resolves. Its damage is Force instead of its normal type.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The weapon's damage increases by 1d4 for each slot level above 2. With a level 5 or higher slot, the duration is 8 hours.","Extract Iron":"Self. Material: a rusty knife. To cast this spell you must expend three Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Roll the expended dice and draw a number of pounds of iron from your blood equal to the total. You shape this iron into nonmagical metal objects whose combined weight cannot exceed the number rolled. The objects are poor in quality but functional.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die and create more iron for each slot level above 3.","Fiend Flesh":"Touch, Concentration up to 1 hour. You touch a willing creature and turn its skin to red scales. Until the spell ends, the target has Resistance to Cold, Fire and Lightning damage and Immunity to Poison damage.","Flash Fever":"Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. Choose a creature you can see within range. It breaks into a cold sweat and makes a Constitution save. On a fail, the sweat becomes a burning fever and the creature takes 4d6 Fire damage. On a success, the spell ends.\n\n**Ongoing fever.** For the duration, the target takes 2d6 Fire damage at the start of each of its turns. It repeats the Constitution save at the end of each of its turns until it has three successes or three failures. Three successes end the spell. Three failures deal 8d6 Fire damage to it and end the spell.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The initial damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3.","Flense":"Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. Using necromantic force, you strip the skin from a creature you can see within range. Make a ranged spell attack against it. On a hit, the target takes 8d6 Necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one.\n\n**Repeating.** On each of your turns until the spell ends, you can take a Magic action to make the same target take a Constitution save. It takes 8d6 Necrotic damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Ending.** The spell ends if the target moves out of range, is reduced to 0 Hit Points, or you can no longer see it.","Fleshcrawl":"Range 100 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. You rip the flesh from a creature and shape it into a twisted mass of blood and skin that attacks that creature. A creature you can see within range makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 8d10 Necrotic damage, and its flayed skin is animated as a grotesque copy using the Fleshling Construct stat block. On a success it takes half as much damage only.\n\n**The fleshling.** It is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action needed from you). If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the slot's level as the spell level in the stat block.","Frightful Start":"Range 30 ft, 1 round. You twist your face to scare a creature you can see within range. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom save or have the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn.","Ghost Light":"Touch, 1 hour. You touch one object no larger than 10 feet in any dimension and name any number of creatures you can see within 10 feet. Until the spell ends, the object sheds silvery Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for another 20 feet. Only the creatures you named when casting can see this light. Everyone else sees the area as they normally would.","Greater Animate Dead":"Range 10 ft. Material: a drop of blood, a piece of flesh, a pinch of bone dust and a black onyx stone worth 75+ GP for each level of CR you animate. Choose corpses within range. You can reanimate up to 5 Undead creatures of Challenge Rating 2 or lower from them.\n\n**Commanding.** On each of your turns you can take a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature made with this spell that is within 120 feet of you. With several creatures you can command any or all of them and give each the same order. You decide its action and movement for its next turn, or you can give a general order such as guarding a room or corridor. With no orders, it only defends itself against hostile creatures. Once given an order, it follows it until the task is done.\n\n**Control.** The creature is under your control for 24 hours, then stops obeying you. To keep control for another 24 hours, you must cast this spell on it again before the current period ends. This use reasserts control over up to four creatures you animated with this spell rather than animating a new one, and it needs no components with a GP cost.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can animate one more Undead creature for each slot level above 5.","Heartseeker":"Range 300 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. Material: a ruby worth 100+ GP. To cast this spell you must expend six Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Your blood flows out and crystallizes into a barbed arrow that you fire at a creature. Make a ranged spell attack against a target within range. On a hit, roll the Hit Point Dice you expended. The creature takes Piercing damage equal to the total.\n\n**Burrowing arrow.** The arrow stays lodged and burrows toward the creature's heart, leaving it open to injury. Until the spell ends, the first successful attack against the creature after its turn ends each round is automatically a Critical Hit.\n\n**Saves.** The target makes a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns. On a fail the effect continues. On a success the creature takes 3d8 Necrotic damage and the spell ends.","Holy Word":"Range 60 ft. You whisper a divine word, careful not to speak loudly, since such celestial power is not for the unworthy. Make a ranged spell attack against a target within range. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 Radiant damage. If the target is a Fey, Fiend or Undead, its Speed is also reduced by 10 feet and it cannot take Reactions until the end of its next turn.\n\n**Cantrip Upgrade.** The damage increases by 1d8 at levels 5 (2d8), 11 (3d8) and 17 (4d8).","Hunter Sense":"Touch, Concentration up to 1 minute. You touch a willing creature and sharpen its senses. For the duration, whenever the target makes a Wisdom (Perception) check, it can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.","Illusory Instrument":"Touch a mundane musical instrument you know and conjure an illusory copy shaped by your fondest memory of it. The copy acts like the real thing but weighs nothing and only you can touch it. It works as a Spellcasting Focus. It vanishes if you move 10 ft away from it, or when you end the spell (no action). As a Bonus Action you can have it do one of these. **Mimic.** Imitate a basic everyday sound such as a bird, footsteps or a slamming door. **Beat.** Play a simple beat at the tempo you choose. **Loop.** Record whatever is played on it and replay it on a loop. **Record.** Record and replay any noise it can pick up within 15 ft, such as conversation or a royal decree.","Incite Riot":"Wave the red handkerchief and choose any number of creatures within 30 ft that can see you. Each makes a Wisdom save, with Advantage if you or your allies are fighting it. On a fail it is Charmed until the spell ends or until you or your allies damage it. A Charmed creature is Friendly to you and your allies. On its turn it must use its action to make melee attacks against the nearest creature that is not you or your allies, or else use its turn to move toward the nearest such target. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on itself on a success.","Intaglio":"Touch a surface for the duration. As a Magic action, trace your hand over non-magical text or an image on a surface within range and copy it onto a new medium you provide, such as a book or parchment. Each Magic action copies one page. When you copy a spellbook this way, use the normal rules for replacing a spellbook, but both the time and the GP cost are halved.","Investiture of Venom":"Your veins swell green and your eyes weep poison. For the duration you gain these benefits. **Immunity.** You have Immunity to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition. **Sense.** You can tell which creatures you see within 30 ft have Resistance or Immunity to Poison damage or Immunity to the Poisoned condition. **Strip.** As a Bonus Action, pick a creature you see within 30 ft. It makes a Constitution save against your spell save DC. On a fail it loses Resistance to Poison damage, Immunity to Poison damage, or Immunity to the Poisoned condition (your choice of which one it has) until the end of your next turn. **Venom Blast.** As a Magic action, venom blasts from you in a Line 15 ft long and 5 ft wide. Each creature in it makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 4d6 Poison damage and is Poisoned until the end of your next turn. On a success it takes half damage only.","Life Tether":"Choose a creature you see within 120 ft. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail a sickly green tether links you and it. Whenever you take damage, the tethered target takes half as much (round down) as Necrotic damage. If the target drops to 0 HP before the spell ends, you can use a Bonus Action to move the tether to a new creature you see within range. The new target must succeed on a Wisdom save or be tethered. Using a higher slot: you can make more tethers at slot level 4 (two tethers), 6 (three tethers) or 8 (four tethers).","Lifesink":"An aura spreads from you in a 15-ft Emanation for the duration. Any other creature that enters the area or starts its turn there takes 4d6 Necrotic damage. At the start of your turn you regain 4d6 HP plus 1 for each creature in the area.","Little Death":"Casting this spell drops you to 0 HP and you die. At the start of your next turn you become a Ghost in the same space as your corpse. Your statistics are replaced by the Ghost stat block, but you keep your HP, Hit Point Dice, Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma scores, and languages. As a Ghost you can only use the abilities in the Ghost stat block, and you add your Proficiency Bonus to its attack rolls and ability DCs. The GM secretly rolls 1d8 when you cast the spell. When that many hours have passed, the spell ends. It ends early if you are reduced to 0 HP as a Ghost or take the Magic action to end it. **Return.** If the Material component (an item of personal sentimental value worth 1+ SP) is still on your corpse when the spell ends, you return to life with HP equal to half your HP maximum. If it is no longer there, you die. **Ruined body.** If your body is destroyed or damaged beyond survival while the spell is active, the duration becomes permanent. You stay a Ghost until your body is targeted by an effect that returns the dead to life such as Raise Dead or Resurrection.","Maelfa's Quickened Class":"Give a short lecture on a topic of your choice to 10 willing creatures within 30 ft. Choose one spell you know or have prepared, one skill you are proficient in, or one language you can speak, read and write. Each target is temporarily given part of your knowledge. **Spell.** Each target prepares the spell, it counts as on their spell list, and it does not count against their prepared spells. **Skill.** Each target gains proficiency in it. **Language.** Each target can speak, read and write it. The knowledge is lost when the spell ends. If a creature is targeted again while still under an earlier casting, the earlier casting ends. Using a higher slot: duration rises to 30 days at slot level 3 or 4, 10 days at 5 or 6, 30 days at 7 or 8, and 1 year at 9.","Magic Mirror":"A bubble of iridescent energy flickers between you and a foe. The triggering spell is redirected to a creature of your choice that you see within 60 ft. If the spell is level 5 or lower, you stop being a target and the chosen creature is the target instead. If the spell is level 6 or higher, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus the spell's level. On a success you stop being a target and the chosen creature is instead. On a failure you remain the target.","Melting Curse":"Target a creature you see within 100 ft and a metal object it holds or wears. The creature makes a Dexterity save, with Advantage if the object is magical. On a fail it takes 5d8 Fire damage and the object melts and oozes to the ground, where it returns to its normal shape and temperature. If the creature tries to pick up or touch the object for the duration, the object heats and melts again and the creature takes 5d8 Fire damage. The object returns to normal once the creature is no longer touching it or the spell ends. Using a higher slot: +1d8 for each slot level above 6.","Mirror Spell":"Try to copy and cast a spell of level 3 or lower that you see being cast within 60 ft. You can only copy spells cast by creatures and cannot copy your own. If the triggering spell is level 2 or lower you copy and cast it automatically. If it is level 3 or higher, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus the triggering spell's level, and you copy it only on a success. The copied spell costs no slot and needs no components. Treat yourself as its original caster, using your own spellcasting ability modifier and spell save DC, and cast it at the lowest level it can be cast. Using a higher slot: the level of the slot you use is the maximum spell level you can copy and cast.","Mortality":"As part of casting you must expend five Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Roll the dice you spent, then choose an Aberration, Celestial, Elemental, Fey or Fiend within 120 ft and condemn it to a taste of mortality. It makes a Charisma save. On a fail its HP maximum and current HP are both reduced by the total you rolled. For the duration, a creature that failed loses all damage Immunities and Resistances, its creature type becomes Humanoid, and it takes an extra 1d4 Necrotic damage each time it takes damage. If an affected creature is reduced to 0 HP, the changes become permanent and the creature dies. That final effect can only be undone by restoring the creature to life and then targeting it with Remove Curse or similar magic. The Material component is a humanoid skull encrusted with gems worth 200+ GP.","Neutralize Aura":"Touch a willing creature and neutralize its aura. Until the spell ends, Fey, Fiends, Celestials and Undead cannot perceive the target. The spell ends early the moment the target makes an attack roll, deals damage, casts a spell, or moves within 5 ft of a creature of one of those types. Using a higher slot: one additional target for each slot level above 1. Casting time is 1 minute.","Overgrow":"Choose a creature or an unworn, uncarried object that is Huge or smaller within 60 ft. Vines grow around it. **Creature.** It makes a Strength save or is Restrained until the spell ends. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. **Object.** It cannot be moved from its spot, and creatures climbing it spend no extra movement. A creature can make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to wrest the object out of the vines so it can be moved. If the object is too heavy for it to move, the attempt fails. Using a higher slot: one additional target for each slot level above 2.","Perfection":"Speak a holy word and remake a creature you see within 60 ft in the image of the Arch Seraphs. The Poisoned condition ends on it, curses on it are suppressed for the duration, and it is restored to its HP maximum. Each of its ability scores below 18 becomes 18. Depending on the word you use, you also grant a blessing from one Arch Seraph. **Aphaelon.** Immunity to the Charmed condition. When it fails a saving throw it can use a Reaction to reroll and must use the new roll. **Empyreus.** Immunity to the Frightened condition, and it deals an extra 4d6 Force damage to the first target it hits on each of its turns. **Miklas.** Immunity to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition, and it regains 4d6 HP at the start of each of its turns. **Morael.** It gains 30 Temporary HP. When an ally within 60 ft of it takes damage, it can use a Reaction to take that damage instead. **Solyma.** Immunity to Thunder damage. When it takes damage from a creature it sees, it can use a Reaction to deal Fire damage to that creature equal to the triggering damage. **Zabriel.** Truesight with a range of 60 ft. At the end of each of its turns it can give Heroic Inspiration to an ally who does not have it.","Phoenix Flames":"You immolate yourself in a cloud of holy flames. You drop to 0 HP and die, and burning radiance erupts from you in a 30-ft Emanation. Each creature in the area makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 30d6 Radiant damage and gains 1 Exhaustion level. On a success it takes half damage only. A creature reduced to 0 HP by this damage is incinerated along with everything nonmagical it wears and carries, and it can be revived only by True Resurrection or Wish. After 10 minutes you rise from the ashes where you cast the spell, returning to life as if targeted by True Resurrection.","Power Word Maim":"Command a creature you see within 60 ft to twist and warp. If it has 125 HP or fewer, it takes 8d10 Necrotic damage and is Prone. If it has more, its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn. The target makes a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns, ending the condition on a success.","Preserve":"Place food and other perishable items weighing 5 lb or less in a sack (holding a pinch of salt) that you touch. For 12 hours they do not age or decay.","Primordial Power":"Grant a creature you touch a share of elemental power. For the duration it can speak and understand Primordial and gains the benefits of the element you choose. **Air.** Resistance to Lightning and Thunder damage and a Fly Speed of 30 ft. **Coldfire.** Resistance to Cold damage. As a Bonus Action it can expend a Hit Point Die to regain HP equal to the roll plus its Constitution modifier. When it takes Fire damage, it cannot use this Bonus Action on its next turn. **Earth.** Advantage on saves against being moved or knocked Prone, and Tremorsense with a range of 30 ft. **Fire.** Resistance to Fire damage. When a creature within 5 ft of it damages it, it can use a Reaction to make one melee attack against that creature with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike. **Water.** Resistance to Acid damage, the ability to breathe underwater, and a Swim Speed of 60 ft.","Reanimate":"As part of casting you must expend three Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Touch a creature that died within the last 10 minutes and return it to life with 1 HP. Roll the dice you spent and the creature gains Temporary HP equal to the roll. At the start of each of its turns it loses 1 of those Temporary HP. While it has Temporary HP from this spell it moves with unnatural vigor and gets a +2 bonus to D20 Tests. When those Temporary HP are gone, it gains 1 Exhaustion level. The spell cannot revive a creature that died of old age and does not restore missing body parts. The Material component is a mix of wilted daisies and herbal powders worth 300+ GP, which the spell consumes.","Red Rain":"As part of casting you must expend eight Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Over 1d6 times 5 minutes the sky darkens and thick blood rains everywhere within 5 miles of you. Each Beast and Plant in the area must succeed on a Wisdom save or be Frightened until it has spent 1 minute outside the area. Mundane plants exposed to the rain wither and die after 10 minutes. For every 10 minutes a creature of any type is directly exposed, it gains 1 Exhaustion level and takes 2d10 Necrotic damage, and its HP maximum drops by the Necrotic damage dealt. That reduction lasts until it removes all Exhaustion levels gained from this spell. While it has any such level, it automatically fails saves to end the Poisoned condition. When the spell ends, roll the Hit Point Dice you spent. Beasts and Plants do not return and plants do not regrow in the area for a number of days equal to the total.","Ride the Lightning":"Turn yourself into a bolt of lightning and create a 5-ft-wide Line between your space and an unoccupied space within 60 ft. Each creature in the Line makes a Dexterity save, taking 4d6 Lightning damage on a fail or half as much on a success. You then reappear in the chosen space. Using a higher slot: +1d6 damage and +10 ft maximum Line length for each slot level above 4.","Sanguine Fusillade":"Crystallize a foe's blood into razor darts. As part of casting you must expend seven Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Roll the dice you spent. A creature you see within 60 ft takes Piercing damage equal to the total. When it takes this damage, seven crimson darts burst from it. You can direct each dart at a creature within 60 ft of the original target, one or several, including the original. The darts strike at once. Make a ranged spell attack for each dart. On a hit, roll one of the Hit Point Dice you spent, and the creature takes Piercing damage equal to the number rolled. Using a higher slot: expend one extra Hit Point Die and create one extra dart for each slot level above 7.","Sanguine Poppet":"As part of casting you must expend three Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Smear the Material component (an object shaped like a creature worth 1+ CP) with your blood. It becomes a poppet under your control. Its AC equals 10 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your spellcasting ability modifier, and it has 30 HP. The spell ends if the poppet drops to 0 HP or is more than 1 mile from you. As a Bonus Action you can command it to move 30 ft, and you see and hear through it until the start of your next turn. As a Magic action you can make it burst in a blood explosion, which ends the spell. Roll the dice you spent. Each creature in a 30-ft-radius Sphere centered on the poppet makes a Dexterity save, taking Necrotic damage equal to the roll on a fail or half as much on a success. Using a higher slot: expend one extra Hit Point Die and gain +1 hour of duration for each slot level above 3.","Sanguine Shield":"As part of casting you must expend two Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Draw lifeforce from the injured around you into a swirling blood shield. You gain 5 Temporary HP for each creature within 30 ft that is below its HP maximum (including you), up to 15. While you have Temporary HP from this spell, you have Cover. When the spell ends, all Temporary HP from it are lost. Using a higher slot: the maximum rises by 5 for each two slot levels above 2.","Seal Spellcasting":"Choose a creature you see within 60 ft. When the target next casts a spell, it must make a Charisma save. On a fail it spends the spell slot and casts as normal, but the spell has no effect. On a success it casts the spell and takes 3d8 Force damage. The spell ends immediately after the creature makes this save. Using a higher slot: +1d8 damage for each slot level above 2.","Sense Lifeblood":"As part of casting you must expend two Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. The lifeblood in creatures tells you its secrets. Creatures with Immunity to the Exhaustion condition are immune to this spell. Until the spell ends you can tell whether creatures you see are biologically related. You also know whether a creature's HP is at maximum, below maximum, at half, or below half. Once on each of your turns when you hit a Bloodied creature with an attack roll using a weapon, an Unarmed Strike or a spell, the target takes extra Necrotic damage equal to a roll of one of the Hit Point Dice you spent. Using a higher slot: Concentration can last up to 1 hour at slot level 3 or 4, and up to 8 hours at 5 or higher.","Serpent Tongue":"Turn your tongue into a venomous serpent for the duration. As a Bonus Action, make a melee spell attack against a creature within 10 ft. On a hit it takes 1d12 Piercing damage and is Poisoned for the rest of the spell. Using a higher slot: +1d12 damage for each slot level above 3.","Shared Judgement":"Once on each of your turns when you reduce an Undead to 0 HP, you can deal 5d6 Radiant damage to a creature you see within 60 ft of you, with no action required. Using a higher slot: +1d6 damage for each slot level above 4.","Shroud Blood":"As part of casting you must expend one Hit Point Die or the spell fails. Choose yourself or a willing creature within 30 ft. The target has Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. When the target loses the Invisible condition, it can use a Reaction to become Invisible again for a number of rounds equal to the Hit Point Dice you spent. It loses the Invisible condition right after it makes an attack roll, deals damage or casts a spell. Using a higher slot: one additional target for each slot level above 1.","Somnolence":"As part of casting you must expend one Hit Point Die or the spell fails. Roll the die you spent plus 2d12 and choose a creature within 30 ft. If the total is equal to or greater than its current HP, it falls into a magical slumber for 1 minute. If the total is equal to or greater than its HP maximum, the slumber lasts 24 hours. The spell ends on a target if it takes damage or someone within 5 ft takes an action to shake it awake. A creature woken early gains 1 Exhaustion level. Creatures that do not sleep, such as elves, and creatures with Immunity to the Exhaustion condition automatically succeed on saves against this spell. **The Long Sleep.** The Prismatic Circle uses a variant that takes 10 minutes and a Humanoid sacrifice. Its adherents believe the ritual holds back the waking of Gormadraug for a day and a night. Using a higher slot: roll an extra 1d12 and expend two additional Hit Point Dice for each slot level above 1.","Spirit Swarm":"Invite spirits to take revenge on a creature you see within 120 ft. The target must have a Charisma of 3 or higher. It makes a Charisma save. On a fail it takes 8d8 Psychic damage and is Frightened until the spell ends. On a success it takes half damage only.","Splattering Smite":"Your strikes drink the blood of your foes. As part of casting you must expend five Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a Melee weapon or an Unarmed Strike, roll one of the Hit Point Dice you spent and regain HP equal to the number rolled.","Steal Immortality":"As part of casting you must expend nine Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Roll the dice you spent and gain Temporary HP equal to twice the total. You gain the creature type of the spell's target in addition to your own. While the spell lasts you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition, you no longer need to eat, drink or breathe, and you have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. You also gain a benefit based on the new type. **Celestial.** Resistance to Radiant and Necrotic damage and a Fly Speed of 60 ft. **Elemental.** Resistance to Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning and Thunder damage. **Fey.** As a Bonus Action, become Invisible until the start of your next turn, or teleport up to 60 ft to an unoccupied space you see. **Fiend.** Resistance to Cold and Fire damage and a Fly Speed of 60 ft. **Undead.** Immunity to Necrotic damage and to the Charmed and Frightened conditions. You keep the creature type and benefits until you cast the spell again or drop to 0 HP. Range 300 ft. The Material component is a gem-encrusted humanoid skull worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes.","Suffocate":"Create a pair of grasping hands of invisible force and make a ranged spell attack against a creature you see within 60 ft. On a hit it is Restrained, and while Restrained it cannot breathe. A creature can hold its breath for rounds equal to 1 plus its Constitution modifier (minimum 30 seconds) before suffocation begins. When it runs out of breath, it gains 1 Exhaustion level at the end of each of its turns. When it can breathe again, it removes all Exhaustion levels gained from suffocating. A creature Restrained by the hands can use an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC and is freed on a success.","Summon Plant (Grim Hollow)":"Call forth a plant spirit in an unoccupied space you see within 90 ft. It uses the Plant Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose a floral feature: Blooming, Oaken or Thorny. The feature determines one of the traits in the stat block. The creature disappears at 0 HP or when the spell ends. It is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required). If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its move to avoid danger. The Material component is a ceramic pot of herbs and fertilizer worth at least 200 GP. Using a higher slot: use the slot's level as the spell level in the stat block.","Summon Sea Spirit":"Call forth an abyssal spirit in an unoccupied space you see within 90 ft. It uses the Sea Serpent Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose an abhorrent feature: Enormous Mouth, Glowing Lantern or Scaled Wings. The feature determines one of the traits in the stat block. The creature disappears at 0 HP or when the spell ends. It is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required). If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its move to avoid danger. The Material component is a bejeweled sea serpent statuette worth at least 300 GP. Using a higher slot: use the slot's level as the spell level in the stat block.","Supernal Smite":"A strike makes the ambient magic around a creature collapse and detonate. The target you hit takes an extra 4d6 Force damage from the attack. If it is concentrating on a spell, that Concentration is broken. Each ongoing spell of level 3 or lower on the target ends. For each ongoing spell of level 4 or higher on it, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus that spell's level. On a success the spell ends.","Theft of Vitae":"Roll one of the Hit Point Dice you expended to cast the spell. The triggering creature takes Necrotic damage equal to the result. You gain Temporary HP equal to the result plus the triggering damage, to a maximum of 15. Using a higher slot: the maximum rises by 10 for each slot level above 2.","Thorn Armor":"A flexible, thorny exoskeleton appears around a willing target you touch. It gains 3d6 Temporary HP. If a creature hits the target with a melee attack roll before the spell ends, that creature takes Piercing damage equal to the number of Temporary HP lost from the attack. The spell ends early if the target has no Temporary HP left from it. Using a higher slot: +2d6 Temporary HP for each slot level above 1.","Tremor":"The ground in a 15-ft Emanation around you shakes violently. You are unaffected. The area is Difficult Terrain. Whenever the Emanation enters a creature's space, a creature enters the Emanation, or a creature ends its turn there, it makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 1d6 Bludgeoning damage and is Prone. A creature makes this save only once per turn. Using a higher slot: +1d6 damage for each slot level above 1.","Undead Enthrallment":"Choose a corpse or several within 10 ft that together match the size of the creature you are animating (the GM decides how many corpses are needed). The spell raises them as Undead creatures of CR 3 or lower, and the GM has their statistics. On each of your turns you can use a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature made by this spell that is within 60 ft of you. You can command any or all of them at once with the same command. You decide its action and movement for its next turn, or give a general order such as guarding a room or corridor. With no command it takes the Dodge action. It keeps following an order until the task is done. The creature obeys you for 24 hours. To keep control for another 24 hours, recast the spell on it before the period ends. That casting renews control of 1 creature already animated by this spell instead of animating a new one. A creature you have kept for 30 days stays under your control permanently. You can control at most four creatures with this spell. The Material components are a clay pot of brackish water, a clay pot of grave dirt, and a black onyx stone worth 500+ GP for each corpse.","Vampiric Claws":"You sprout wicked claws. When your Unarmed Strike deals damage with them, it deals 1d6 Slashing damage instead of its normal damage, and you use your spellcasting ability modifier for the attack and damage rolls instead of Strength. While the spell lasts, each time you deal damage with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary HP equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. Those Temporary HP are lost when the spell ends.","Vibrating Humors":"As part of casting you must expend one Hit Point Die or the spell fails. A creature you see within 30 ft makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes Thunder damage equal to a roll of the die you spent and has Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks because its blood hums loudly. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success. Using a higher slot: expend one additional Hit Point Die for each slot level above 1 to increase the damage.","Viscous Sheath":"As part of casting you must expend seven Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Clotted blood wraps your body. Whenever a creature within 5 ft hits you with a melee attack roll, it takes Necrotic damage equal to a roll of one of the dice you spent plus your spellcasting ability modifier. When a creature hits you with a Melee weapon, you can use a Reaction to make clots form around the weapon. The attacker must succeed on a Strength save or the weapon sticks to you. While the weapon is stuck, it cannot be used, and the attacker is Grappled unless it releases the weapon. The attacker can use an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to free the weapon, or release the weapon to end the Grappled condition. You can trap a number of weapons equal to the Hit Point Dice you spent. When the spell ends the weapons are released. The Material component is a bloody funerary shroud. Using a higher slot: trap one additional weapon for each slot level above 4.","Wall of Gloom":"Create a wall of swirling gray energy made of the psychic pain of loss, on a solid surface within 120 ft. Make it up to 60 ft long, 10 ft high and 5 ft thick, or a ring with a 20-ft diameter, up to 20 ft high and 5 ft thick. The wall blocks line of sight and sheds Dim Light out to 100 ft. When you cast it, you and creatures you designate can pass through and stay near it unharmed. Any other creature that moves within 20 ft of it or starts its turn there must succeed on a Charisma save or be Incapacitated until the start of its next turn. A creature can move through the wall, but it is emotionally draining. The first time a creature enters the wall on a turn or ends its turn in it, it must succeed on a Charisma save or gain 1 Exhaustion level.","Weave Numen":"You sense magic within 120 ft. You see a faint aura around any visible creature or object there that bears magic and learn its school of magic, if any. You also gain thirteen threads. Spend them as follows. **Enhance.** When you cast a spell, spend 1 thread (no action) to enhance it as if you had used a slot 1 level higher, and gain Temporary HP equal to 1 plus the spell's level. **Interrupt.** When a creature you see within 120 ft casts a spell, spend 1 thread as a Reaction to interrupt it. A spell of level 3 or lower fails with no effect. For a spell of level 4 or higher, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus the spell's level, and on a success the spell fails with no effect. **Amplify.** When you cast a spell that heals or damages a creature, spend up to six threads (no action). The healing or damage to one creature increases by four times the threads spent. You lose any remaining threads when the spell ends, and the spell ends if you spend them all. The Material component is a mithral sewing needle worth 300+ GP, which the spell consumes. Using a higher slot: gain two more threads for each slot level above 6.","Wilting Smite":"As part of casting you must expend two Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. The creature you hit with the strike loses all Resistances to damage until the start of your next turn and takes extra Necrotic damage from the attack. Roll one of the Hit Point Dice you spent to determine the damage.","Wipe Face":"Curse a creature you see within 60 ft. Its face is replaced by smooth skin that seals its eyes, nose and mouth. It is Blinded and Incapacitated and begins suffocating. At the end of each of its turns it can make a Constitution save to end the spell. Dealing at least 15 Slashing damage to it opens an airway so it can breathe, but the curse seals the opening again at the start of your next turn.","Wrack":"Choose a creature you see within 30 ft. It must succeed on a Constitution save or suffer painful muscle spasms for the duration. On a fail its Speed is halved and it has Disadvantage on attack rolls. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success."};
var IT=[["Hunter's Armor","Armor","Common",0,"Any Light, Medium or Heavy armor can be made as Hunter's Armor for 500 gp more than its base price. Adamantine and mithral threads turn the worst blows into normal wounds. When a blow would cause a Grievous Wound, roll a d20. On an 11 or higher, no Grievous Wound results.",{}]];
